WEBVTT

1
00:00:58,041 --> 00:01:00,791
(muffled breathing)

2
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:24,291
(beeps)

3
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:57,708
(beeps)

4
00:01:57,791 --> 00:02:00,375
(all beeping)

5
00:02:12,916 --> 00:02:15,708
(♪ adventurous music playing)

6
00:02:15,791 --> 00:02:18,416
(birds squawking)

7
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:23,958
(wailing sound plays)

8
00:02:52,791 --> 00:02:55,083
(♪ enchanting music playing)

9
00:03:00,791 --> 00:03:02,375
Star.

10
00:03:05,916 --> 00:03:07,583
Comm… Command.

11
00:03:11,125 --> 00:03:12,333
Star.

12
00:03:12,916 --> 00:03:14,208
Command.

13
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:17,375
(all) Star. Command.

14
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:18,750
- Rendezvous!
- With!

15
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:19,958
(all) Star Command.

16
00:03:20,041 --> 00:03:22,375
Rendezvous with Star Command.

17
00:03:22,458 --> 00:03:24,583
Rendezvous with Star Command.

18
00:03:24,666 --> 00:03:26,583
Rendezvous with Star Command.

19
00:03:26,666 --> 00:03:29,000
Rendezvous with Star Command.

20
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,375
Rendezvous with Star Command.

21
00:03:31,458 --> 00:03:33,875
Rendezvous with Star Command.

22
00:03:33,958 --> 00:03:36,208
Rendezvous with Star Command.

23
00:03:36,291 --> 00:03:38,333
Rendezvous with Star Command.

24
00:04:00,041 --> 00:04:01,166
There.

25
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:06,208
This way, you'll never lose me, Jessie.

26
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:10,166
<i>Friends forever, partner.</i>

27
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,375
(giggles)

28
00:04:11,458 --> 00:04:13,125
That's right, partner.

29
00:04:13,208 --> 00:04:16,458
But don't you worry.
I'll keep a good eye on you.

30
00:04:16,541 --> 00:04:17,625
(grunts)

31
00:04:19,541 --> 00:04:22,375
See? I'm still watching.

32
00:04:22,458 --> 00:04:23,666
(giggles)

33
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:26,666
I'm gone… (gasps) …but I'm back.

34
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:29,708
I'm gone. (gasps) I'm back.

35
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,208
I still see you.

36
00:04:32,291 --> 00:04:35,083
(gasps) Oh, no. (echoing) I'm gone.

37
00:04:37,583 --> 00:04:40,625
And I will love you all the time…

38
00:04:40,708 --> 00:04:43,875
even when I'm mad or sad

39
00:04:43,958 --> 00:04:46,041
or leave you outside by accident.

40
00:04:46,125 --> 00:04:48,166
I'll still love you forever.

41
00:04:48,916 --> 00:04:50,416
(as Jessie) Really? You mean it?

42
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,125
Forever and ever and ever?

43
00:04:52,208 --> 00:04:54,625
Yep. All the evers.

44
00:04:54,708 --> 00:04:57,708
Then do you, Forky, take Karen Beverly

45
00:04:57,791 --> 00:05:00,041
to be your beloved bride?

46
00:05:00,125 --> 00:05:01,416
(as Forky) I do.

47
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:03,250
And do you, Karen Beverly?

48
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:04,416
(as Karen Beverly) I do.

49
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:06,541
(sobs, blows nose)

50
00:05:07,666 --> 00:05:09,083
(giggles)

51
00:05:09,166 --> 00:05:11,125
Yeehaw!

52
00:05:11,208 --> 00:05:13,625
I now pronounce you husband…

53
00:05:13,708 --> 00:05:15,750
and knife.

54
00:05:16,375 --> 00:05:18,166
(kissing)

55
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:19,791
Kissy, kissy.

56
00:05:19,875 --> 00:05:22,166
- (kissing continues)
- (gasps)

57
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:23,625
(chuckles)

58
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:28,125
(gasps) Who poisoned the maid of honor?

59
00:05:28,208 --> 00:05:29,375
(shouts, groans)

60
00:05:29,458 --> 00:05:31,250
- (shouts)
- (all gasp)

61
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:32,708
- (gasps)
- (screaming)

62
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:38,166
Oh! Why? Why?

63
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:39,458
Everyone!

64
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:42,791
Step aside. I know CPR.

65
00:05:42,875 --> 00:05:44,625
One, two, three.

66
00:05:45,125 --> 00:05:48,250
Now, the kiss of life.

67
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:49,333
(gasps)

68
00:05:49,416 --> 00:05:51,375
(inhales deeply, blows)

69
00:05:55,958 --> 00:05:56,958
Oh.

70
00:05:57,041 --> 00:05:58,708
(inhales deeply, blows)

71
00:05:58,791 --> 00:06:01,625
- (inhales deeply)
- (car approaching)

72
00:06:03,583 --> 00:06:04,625
(child 1 chuckling)

73
00:06:04,708 --> 00:06:06,666
(child 2) You're so funny.

74
00:06:09,916 --> 00:06:11,875
But we didn't solve my murder.

75
00:06:11,958 --> 00:06:14,166
Just hold your horses, Rex.

76
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:15,958
Psst. Dolly, what's going on?

77
00:06:16,041 --> 00:06:17,750
(sighs) Not sure.

78
00:06:17,833 --> 00:06:19,125
You know, at first I was mad

79
00:06:19,208 --> 00:06:20,416
Bonnie drew these glasses on me,

80
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,333
but honestly, I can see
so much better now.

81
00:06:22,416 --> 00:06:23,916
Dolly, focus.

82
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Oh! Sorry.

83
00:06:25,083 --> 00:06:27,208
It's the Jordan twins. They're back home.

84
00:06:27,291 --> 00:06:30,500
(twins chattering)

85
00:06:30,583 --> 00:06:32,916
(laughing)

86
00:06:33,833 --> 00:06:37,000
Poor thing. She's still afraid
to ask them to play.

87
00:06:37,791 --> 00:06:39,500
Not this time. (grunts)

88
00:06:41,583 --> 00:06:42,625
(chattering continues)

89
00:06:42,708 --> 00:06:43,708
(Jessie grunts)

90
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:46,791
<i>Giddy-up there! Time's a-wastin'!</i>

91
00:06:46,875 --> 00:06:48,125
(gasps) Oh, no.

92
00:06:54,166 --> 00:06:55,291
(twins laughing)

93
00:06:58,083 --> 00:06:59,750
That's it, Bonnie.

94
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:01,083
You can do it.

95
00:07:11,916 --> 00:07:12,958
(Bonnie gasps)

96
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:17,083
(as Jessie) Hello.

97
00:07:18,541 --> 00:07:21,125
(twins laugh)

98
00:07:22,416 --> 00:07:23,708
(door closes)

99
00:07:30,291 --> 00:07:32,375
Uh, Jessie. The wedding got me thinking…

100
00:07:32,458 --> 00:07:33,791
Shh. Something's off.

101
00:07:33,875 --> 00:07:36,000
So, how'd the wedding go?

102
00:07:36,083 --> 00:07:37,666
Who murdered the maid of honor this time?

103
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:39,875
Mom? Dad?

104
00:07:39,958 --> 00:07:41,166
Yeah, sweetie?

105
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:45,750
Why won't anyone be my friend?

106
00:07:45,833 --> 00:07:47,208
(all gasp)

107
00:07:47,291 --> 00:07:50,166
- Oh, Bonnie, come here.
- Oh, sweetie.

108
00:07:55,416 --> 00:07:57,041
- Buzz.
- Ow.

109
00:07:57,125 --> 00:07:58,708
You're deputy till I get back.

110
00:07:58,791 --> 00:07:59,875
Me? Right.

111
00:07:59,958 --> 00:08:03,333
I'm gonna get those twins
to play with Bonnie somehow.

112
00:08:03,416 --> 00:08:04,708
Come on, Bullseye.

113
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:08,833
(♪ adventurous music playing)

114
00:08:19,208 --> 00:08:21,208
(♪ ominous music playing)

115
00:08:22,291 --> 00:08:23,291
Huh?

116
00:08:24,458 --> 00:08:27,041
Why, they're… they're both
just sitting there.

117
00:08:28,166 --> 00:08:29,375
Doin' nothing.

118
00:08:30,333 --> 00:08:32,583
They ain't playing with toys at all.

119
00:08:32,666 --> 00:08:34,916
What, you didn't hear?

120
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,666
Uh, n-no, I… I didn't hear.

121
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:38,583
- She didn't hear.
- She didn't hear?

122
00:08:38,666 --> 00:08:40,666
What? What didn't I hear?

123
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,541
The age of toys is over, lass.

124
00:08:42,625 --> 00:08:44,666
What do you mean, "over"?
When did that happen?

125
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:48,000
It's been happening for years.
Where have you been?

126
00:08:48,083 --> 00:08:50,291
(stammers) Across the street, playing.

127
00:08:50,375 --> 00:08:51,625
(all) Playing?

128
00:08:51,708 --> 00:08:53,833
Oh! Your kid still plays?

129
00:08:53,916 --> 00:08:56,666
I don't remember play. Describe it to me.

130
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:59,916
(stammers) Are you guys okay?
What happened to you?

131
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
- (all) Tech!
- Devices!

132
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,875
Everywhere, devices!

133
00:09:03,958 --> 00:09:05,708
Phones! Tablets!

134
00:09:05,791 --> 00:09:07,208
Computers! Cameras!

135
00:09:07,291 --> 00:09:08,708
The screens just took over!

136
00:09:08,791 --> 00:09:10,750
All the tapping. The tapping!

137
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:12,708
Tap, tap, tap, tap.

138
00:09:12,791 --> 00:09:14,583
- Make it stop.
- The tapping. Not the tapping!

139
00:09:14,666 --> 00:09:16,125
Take our advice, darlin'.

140
00:09:16,208 --> 00:09:17,791
Find a drawer and hide,

141
00:09:17,875 --> 00:09:19,458
'cause once tech invades your home,

142
00:09:19,541 --> 00:09:21,125
you're dead where you lie.

143
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:24,958
(chuckles) Oh, well,
it's probably just a fad.

144
00:09:25,041 --> 00:09:28,000
Like, you know, record players
or Hula-Hoops.

145
00:09:28,083 --> 00:09:29,541
You don't get it.

146
00:09:29,625 --> 00:09:31,708
The age of toys is over.

147
00:09:31,791 --> 00:09:32,958
Over.

148
00:09:33,041 --> 00:09:35,375
Tap, tap, tap…

149
00:09:35,458 --> 00:09:39,250
Don't believe us? Come see for yourself.

150
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:44,041
(Jessie groaning, grunting)

151
00:09:45,291 --> 00:09:47,416
- (grunts, gasps)
- (grunts)

152
00:09:48,916 --> 00:09:50,541
(Jessie) Look at 'em all.

153
00:09:51,875 --> 00:09:54,125
All on devices.

154
00:09:56,791 --> 00:09:58,750
Except for Bonnie.

155
00:09:58,833 --> 00:09:59,833
(sighs)

156
00:09:59,916 --> 00:10:02,250
No wonder she can't
make a friend, Bullseye.

157
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:05,625
She's the only one out there
still playing with toys.

158
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:07,541
(sighs)

159
00:10:07,625 --> 00:10:10,708
- Don't worry. We're safe.
- (giggles)

160
00:10:13,708 --> 00:10:15,458
Are we sure about this?

161
00:10:15,541 --> 00:10:18,750
(sighs) No, but I think it might help.

162
00:10:18,833 --> 00:10:20,625
(sighs) Okay.

163
00:10:21,583 --> 00:10:22,416
(phone chimes)

164
00:10:22,958 --> 00:10:23,791
(gasps)

165
00:10:23,875 --> 00:10:27,125
A Lilypad! Oh, thank you, Mom.
Thank you, Dad.

166
00:10:27,208 --> 00:10:29,833
Well, now that you're eight,
we thought you were ready.

167
00:10:32,083 --> 00:10:34,458
<i>Hi, there. I'm Lilypad.</i>
<i>Welcome to The Pond.</i>

168
00:10:34,541 --> 00:10:36,666
You can take today
to figure out how to use it,

169
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:38,375
but then tomorrow, we'll start having

170
00:10:38,458 --> 00:10:40,375
- strict screen time.
- (Bonnie) Uh-huh.

171
00:10:43,541 --> 00:10:44,625
(Bullseye grunts)

172
00:10:46,916 --> 00:10:49,416
(Lilypad beeping)

173
00:10:50,208 --> 00:10:53,333
(chuckles) <i>Uh-oh, try again.</i>

174
00:10:54,375 --> 00:10:55,958
<i>Keep hopping.</i>

175
00:10:56,041 --> 00:10:57,708
(frog croaking)

176
00:10:58,750 --> 00:11:00,541
(beeping continues)

177
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:02,041
<i>Try again.</i>

178
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:12,166
Morning. Screen time's over now.

179
00:11:12,791 --> 00:11:14,666
Let's put Lilypad away
and come to breakfast.

180
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:16,041
Okay.

181
00:11:22,916 --> 00:11:24,333
(Hamm) We can't let that thing replace us.

182
00:11:24,416 --> 00:11:27,291
Jumpin' jelly beans!
Will y'all just settle down?

183
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:30,875
Now, I'm gonna have some words
with this Lilypad

184
00:11:30,958 --> 00:11:32,958
and let her know how
things are run around here.

185
00:11:33,041 --> 00:11:35,416
- Try to stay calm, Jessie.
- Buzz, you know me.

186
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:37,041
I'm the definition of calm.

187
00:11:37,125 --> 00:11:38,291
- (whinnies)
- (Buzz laughs)

188
00:11:38,375 --> 00:11:39,541
That's not gonna work.

189
00:11:39,625 --> 00:11:40,500
(grunts)

190
00:11:44,458 --> 00:11:45,583
(Bullseye grunts)

191
00:11:47,125 --> 00:11:48,500
- Hi!
- What the--

192
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:52,041
Sorry. I didn't mean to scare you.
Sleep mode, you know?

193
00:11:52,125 --> 00:11:53,958
No? Eh, forget it.

194
00:11:54,041 --> 00:11:55,375
I was just gonna hop on the charger.

195
00:11:55,458 --> 00:11:57,041
Battery could use a little refresh.

196
00:11:57,125 --> 00:11:59,833
- I wanna talk to you, device.
- Please, call me "Lily."

197
00:11:59,916 --> 00:12:02,375
Now look here. Me and the toys
have been working all summer

198
00:12:02,458 --> 00:12:05,000
to try and get Bonnie to make
friends with the Jordan twins

199
00:12:05,083 --> 00:12:06,541
- across the street.
- Uh-huh. Yeah.

200
00:12:06,625 --> 00:12:08,250
- Then you had to ruin it…
- Got it.

201
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:09,375
…with all your stupid…

202
00:12:09,458 --> 00:12:10,541
You're not even listening

203
00:12:10,625 --> 00:12:11,500
- to me!
- Oh, no.

204
00:12:11,583 --> 00:12:14,458
I was listening.
I'm always listening. See?

205
00:12:14,541 --> 00:12:16,666
<i>Now look here. Me and the toys</i>
<i>have been working all summer</i>

206
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,500
<i>to try to get Bonnie to make</i>
<i>friends with the Jordan twins.</i>

207
00:12:18,583 --> 00:12:19,750
Now in Spanish.

208
00:12:19,833 --> 00:12:21,583
- (speaking Spanish)
- (all gasp)

209
00:12:22,166 --> 00:12:23,416
- Now as a rap.
- (♪ drumbeat playing)

210
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,125
♪ <i>Me and the toys</i>
<i>Been working all summer </i>♪

211
00:12:25,208 --> 00:12:26,375
♪ <i>Trying to get Bonnie</i>
<i>To make friends </i>♪

212
00:12:26,458 --> 00:12:27,708
Ooh! Our first dance, honey!

213
00:12:27,791 --> 00:12:29,750
Oh, this concerns me ethically.

214
00:12:30,625 --> 00:12:31,625
(♪ drumbeat stops)

215
00:12:31,708 --> 00:12:33,708
Whatever. You don't understand.

216
00:12:33,791 --> 00:12:35,791
Our kid needs to learn
how to make friends,

217
00:12:35,875 --> 00:12:37,750
and your screen ain't helping.

218
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:40,166
Look, if it's friends Bonnie needs,
consider it done.

219
00:12:40,250 --> 00:12:42,083
- (chimes)
- There.

220
00:12:42,166 --> 00:12:44,333
What? (stammers) What happened?

221
00:12:44,416 --> 00:12:46,708
Oh, it was easy. I just
sent a friend request

222
00:12:46,791 --> 00:12:48,625
to all the girls in Bonnie's dance class.

223
00:12:48,708 --> 00:12:50,375
But that's… They're not here.

224
00:12:50,458 --> 00:12:52,833
Oh, yes, they are, silly.

225
00:12:52,916 --> 00:12:55,541
Chelsea, Kara and even Heidi,
they're all here.

226
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:58,166
The parents created
a group chat on The Pond.

227
00:12:58,250 --> 00:12:59,291
You see, on The Pond,

228
00:12:59,375 --> 00:13:01,416
while Bonnie's playing
my fun learning games,

229
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,208
she can also socialize with other kids.

230
00:13:03,291 --> 00:13:06,333
That's why Mom and Dad bought
me. To make connections.

231
00:13:07,708 --> 00:13:10,375
- Voilà! Friend made.
- (all exclaim)

232
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:11,458
I want one.

233
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:14,000
That Lilypad made Bonnie
a friend in, like…

234
00:13:14,083 --> 00:13:15,541
Fifteen seconds. I was counting.

235
00:13:15,625 --> 00:13:17,375
- What? No.
- No touching.

236
00:13:17,458 --> 00:13:20,291
That ain't a friend. A real
friend would actually be here.

237
00:13:20,375 --> 00:13:21,375
Well, that's my point, Jessica.

238
00:13:21,458 --> 00:13:22,291
(gasps)

239
00:13:22,375 --> 00:13:24,041
- Oh, no.
- (Hamm) She used the "J" word.

240
00:13:24,125 --> 00:13:25,125
(Rex) Scandal!

241
00:13:25,208 --> 00:13:27,208
With my help, eventually Bonnie can reach

242
00:13:27,291 --> 00:13:28,791
all of her developmental goals.

243
00:13:28,875 --> 00:13:30,375
I just want what's best for her.

244
00:13:30,458 --> 00:13:32,541
I think I know more
than a green calculator

245
00:13:32,625 --> 00:13:33,875
what's best for Bonnie.

246
00:13:33,958 --> 00:13:35,833
- Uh, really?
- Yeah, really.

247
00:13:35,916 --> 00:13:37,875
I got three kids' worth of know-how.

248
00:13:37,958 --> 00:13:42,541
Bonnie. Before that, Andy,
and before that, Emily.

249
00:13:42,625 --> 00:13:44,583
I think that just means you're old.

250
00:13:44,666 --> 00:13:47,041
Yikes! Wow. Really old.

251
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:48,583
Fine. We'll wrestle for her.

252
00:13:48,666 --> 00:13:50,875
- Hi-yah! Come on!
- Whoa! (chuckling)

253
00:13:50,958 --> 00:13:52,333
Wrestle me, you frog-faced faker.

254
00:13:52,416 --> 00:13:53,500
That kinda tickles.

255
00:13:53,583 --> 00:13:55,083
- I'll knock ya off this bed.
- I thought we were

256
00:13:55,166 --> 00:13:57,166
- staying calm-- Ah!
- Put up a fight, you riffraff.

257
00:13:57,250 --> 00:13:58,750
- Whoa!
- I'll show you who's better

258
00:13:58,833 --> 00:13:59,666
- for Bonnie.
- Okay.

259
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:01,333
Nobody said anything about lifting.

260
00:14:01,416 --> 00:14:03,291
- (Dad) Bonnie?
- (Bonnie) Just a sec.

261
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:14,875
- (Bonnie screams)
- (coughs)

262
00:14:14,958 --> 00:14:15,958
- Mom! Dad!
- Bonnie?

263
00:14:16,041 --> 00:14:17,458
What? (stammers) What's wrong?

264
00:14:17,541 --> 00:14:18,375
Chelsea from dance class

265
00:14:18,458 --> 00:14:19,958
invited me to a sleepover this weekend.

266
00:14:20,041 --> 00:14:22,000
Can I go? Can I go? Can I go?

267
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:24,125
Please!

268
00:14:24,208 --> 00:14:26,041
Well, uh, all right.

269
00:14:26,125 --> 00:14:29,000
As long as we talk to Chelsea's parents,

270
00:14:29,083 --> 00:14:30,416
I guess it's okay.

271
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,416
Yay! Yes!

272
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,458
(Dad) Come on, everybody. Let's eat.

273
00:14:37,875 --> 00:14:39,875
Yeah, I got dibs on behind the dresser.

274
00:14:39,958 --> 00:14:41,166
Should buy me a few years.

275
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:43,500
Ah! Extinction. Not again.

276
00:14:43,583 --> 00:14:45,083
- Called it.
- Don't get me started.

277
00:14:45,166 --> 00:14:48,333
Now, look. Our time ain't over yet.
Bonnie still loves us.

278
00:14:48,416 --> 00:14:49,875
- (Dolly) Really?
- (Jessie) She does.

279
00:14:49,958 --> 00:14:52,583
Sure. Whatever you say, Sheriff.

280
00:14:54,458 --> 00:14:56,083
It's just a phase.

281
00:14:58,375 --> 00:14:59,625
(sighs)

282
00:14:59,708 --> 00:15:01,708
(♪ sentimental music playing)

283
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:14,750
(♪ marching music playing)

284
00:15:26,083 --> 00:15:28,041
(static crackling)

285
00:15:29,875 --> 00:15:30,875
(sighs)

286
00:15:32,083 --> 00:15:35,208
(beeping)

287
00:15:35,291 --> 00:15:37,166
'Ello? Caboom here. Over.

288
00:15:37,250 --> 00:15:39,833
- (Jessie) <i>Oh! Duke.</i>
- Hey there, Red.

289
00:15:39,916 --> 00:15:41,958
- Long time.
<i>- Hey. Um…</i>

290
00:15:42,041 --> 00:15:43,916
<i>- Is Woody there?</i>
- Please hold.

291
00:15:48,416 --> 00:15:50,250
(exclaims) Hey, cowboy!

292
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:52,000
Pump the brakes, Duke, he's mid-rescue.

293
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:54,250
Bad squirrel! No! Yeah, bad!

294
00:15:54,333 --> 00:15:56,500
- Evil squirrel! No!
- Okay, now, Mr. Nutcase.

295
00:15:56,583 --> 00:15:59,208
- Doctor. Doctor.
- Okay, Dr. Nutcase.

296
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:02,125
On three, you're going to unstick yourself

297
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:03,666
- and drop into my arms.
- (sobbing)

298
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:06,416
What's the point? It's over for toys.

299
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:09,958
The screens have won, and now
the squirrel's gonna eat me!

300
00:16:10,041 --> 00:16:11,166
You guys ready?

301
00:16:11,250 --> 00:16:12,958
Just one text, ping,

302
00:16:13,041 --> 00:16:14,916
and Trevor totally forgot
I was stuck in the tree.

303
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,250
(crying) We're doomed!

304
00:16:16,333 --> 00:16:20,125
Okay, one, two…

305
00:16:20,208 --> 00:16:21,333
I give up!

306
00:16:21,416 --> 00:16:22,625
(shouts) Three, three!

307
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,291
I got you. I got you.

308
00:16:26,375 --> 00:16:27,833
(Dr. Nutcase sobbing)

309
00:16:27,916 --> 00:16:31,750
- Okay. It's okay. I got you.
- Let me go! I'm yucky.

310
00:16:32,958 --> 00:16:35,625
- (Woody) <i>Hello, Jessie? Hello?</i>
- (gasps) Woody!

311
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:37,458
Jessie, hey. What's going on?

312
00:16:37,541 --> 00:16:39,125
- Curse technology!
- Hey, quiet down.

313
00:16:39,208 --> 00:16:41,541
(Dr. Nutcase) <i>We're all just landfill now.</i>

314
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:44,875
Woody, is it as bad out there
for toys as they say it is?

315
00:16:44,958 --> 00:16:46,708
- Beware the machines!
- Just let go!

316
00:16:46,791 --> 00:16:48,125
Yeah. Yeah, it's bad.

317
00:16:48,208 --> 00:16:50,458
We're finding
more abandoned toys each day.

318
00:16:50,541 --> 00:16:52,041
Why? Are you guys okay?

319
00:16:52,125 --> 00:16:55,666
Not really. Tech's invaded our house too.

320
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:56,583
(Woody) <i>Oh, no.</i>

321
00:16:56,666 --> 00:16:58,375
Yeah, her name's Lilypad.

322
00:16:58,458 --> 00:17:01,000
Looks like a frog,
but really, she's a leech,

323
00:17:01,083 --> 00:17:03,333
<i>sucking up all of Bonnie's attention.</i>

324
00:17:03,416 --> 00:17:06,541
<i>Making her stare at her screen all day.</i>

325
00:17:06,625 --> 00:17:09,000
<i>There's got to be some way to stop it.</i>

326
00:17:09,083 --> 00:17:11,041
(stammers) I don't know, Jessie. Uh…

327
00:17:11,125 --> 00:17:14,166
Toys are for play, but tech is…

328
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:16,333
<i>it's for everything.</i>

329
00:17:16,416 --> 00:17:17,583
(sighs)

330
00:17:19,125 --> 00:17:22,000
You remember my first kid, Emily?

331
00:17:22,083 --> 00:17:25,541
The one I told you about who gave me away.

332
00:17:25,625 --> 00:17:27,291
(Woody) <i>Course I do, yeah.</i>

333
00:17:27,375 --> 00:17:30,208
It feels like that all over again.

334
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:32,875
<i>First we were playing…</i>

335
00:17:32,958 --> 00:17:33,958
(Emily laughs)

336
00:17:34,041 --> 00:17:36,041
<i>…and then the world started changing.</i>

337
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:38,208
(laughs) I know.

338
00:17:38,291 --> 00:17:40,333
(Jessie) <i>Emily changed and then…</i>

339
00:17:41,250 --> 00:17:42,333
<i>just like that…</i>

340
00:17:43,458 --> 00:17:45,541
<i>my time with her was over.</i>

341
00:17:46,958 --> 00:17:50,291
Now I'm losing Bonnie to this device.

342
00:17:51,625 --> 00:17:53,083
Is it me?

343
00:17:53,583 --> 00:17:56,125
Am I just no good at being a toy?

344
00:17:56,208 --> 00:17:58,166
(Woody) <i>Jessie, you're a good toy.</i>

345
00:17:58,250 --> 00:18:00,583
- I don't know.
- (Woody) <i>Jessie.</i>

346
00:18:02,833 --> 00:18:03,916
(Bullseye grunts)

347
00:18:04,916 --> 00:18:07,708
(inhales sharply) Okay.
Jessie… (clears throat)

348
00:18:07,791 --> 00:18:10,791
No, Sheriff… Sheriff Jessie,
I appreciate this promotion,

349
00:18:10,875 --> 00:18:12,625
but what I'd really like to promote…

350
00:18:12,708 --> 00:18:14,500
No, that is so stupid.

351
00:18:14,583 --> 00:18:15,958
(Bullseye sniffing)

352
00:18:16,750 --> 00:18:19,708
But she got Bonnie invited
to a sleepover in seconds.

353
00:18:19,791 --> 00:18:22,875
(Woody) <i>Jessie, you know</i>
<i>Bonnie better than anyone.</i>

354
00:18:22,958 --> 00:18:24,458
<i>What does your gut say?</i>

355
00:18:30,541 --> 00:18:32,666
- That it can't be that easy.
- (Woody) <i>Mm-hmm.</i>

356
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:33,750
Bonnie won't click

357
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:35,166
- with just anyone.
<i>- Exactly.</i>

358
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:37,750
She needs to actually meet these girls.

359
00:18:37,833 --> 00:18:41,666
She's not like most kids.
Bonnie plays different. She…

360
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:45,333
She needs to play.

361
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,750
- (Woody) <i>Jessie?</i>
- You're right, Woody.

362
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:49,125
Toys are for play.

363
00:18:49,208 --> 00:18:52,041
<i>And play is how</i>
<i>she'll find the right friend.</i>

364
00:18:52,125 --> 00:18:52,958
Okay.

365
00:18:53,041 --> 00:18:55,291
The age of toys may be over,

366
00:18:55,375 --> 00:18:58,291
but I'm gonna do something
useful before I go.

367
00:18:58,375 --> 00:18:59,791
I'm going to that sleepover,

368
00:18:59,875 --> 00:19:02,541
and making a real friend for Bonnie.

369
00:19:02,625 --> 00:19:04,541
- Jessie, are you okay?
- (gasps) Buzz!

370
00:19:04,625 --> 00:19:06,166
- Jessie? Jessie!
- (static on radio)

371
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:07,583
What do you think you're doing?

372
00:19:07,666 --> 00:19:09,708
What are you doing?
I assumed you needed backup.

373
00:19:09,791 --> 00:19:10,833
No! I don't…

374
00:19:10,916 --> 00:19:13,583
<i>Need backup, Deputy.</i>

375
00:19:13,666 --> 00:19:14,666
(gasps)

376
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,375
- (whispers) What happened?
- Why are we whispering?

377
00:19:17,458 --> 00:19:18,458
- He's finally asleep.
- (snoring)

378
00:19:18,541 --> 00:19:19,541
So what's wrong?

379
00:19:19,625 --> 00:19:21,958
I don't know, but you heard Jessie.

380
00:19:22,041 --> 00:19:23,541
She needs a deputy.

381
00:19:23,625 --> 00:19:24,791
(screams) Machines!

382
00:19:24,875 --> 00:19:26,791
- Jessie.
- Yeah, what is it?

383
00:19:26,875 --> 00:19:27,875
Uh…

384
00:19:29,666 --> 00:19:31,666
(stammers) You know…
Never mind. Never mind.

385
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:33,958
If you need anything,
I'm here. At your service.

386
00:19:34,041 --> 00:19:35,666
Okay. Thanks.

387
00:19:36,166 --> 00:19:38,500
Come on, Bullseye.
I'm gonna need your help.

388
00:19:38,583 --> 00:19:39,916
(Bullseye whinnies)

389
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,291
(Buzz sighs)

390
00:19:46,666 --> 00:19:49,166
(♪ adventurous music playing)

391
00:19:59,833 --> 00:20:02,208
We can't see the stars, Buzz.
Too much fog.

392
00:20:02,291 --> 00:20:05,625
Hmm. We need to find higher ground.

393
00:20:06,125 --> 00:20:08,625
- (gasps)
- (all beeping)

394
00:20:17,333 --> 00:20:19,333
(♪ dramatic music playing)

395
00:20:36,875 --> 00:20:37,958
(machinery whirring)

396
00:20:38,041 --> 00:20:39,041
Huh?

397
00:20:49,291 --> 00:20:50,291
A-ha!

398
00:20:59,583 --> 00:21:02,291
Buzz, I have our bearings.
East-north-- (gasps)

399
00:21:10,541 --> 00:21:12,333
I'm not cleaning that up.

400
00:21:16,083 --> 00:21:18,458
- Why did we…
- Freeze?

401
00:21:18,958 --> 00:21:19,958
(all) Fascinating.

402
00:21:20,041 --> 00:21:21,416
- Must…
- Avoid…

403
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,333
Humans.

404
00:21:22,416 --> 00:21:23,583
(all) Affirmative.

405
00:21:23,666 --> 00:21:26,166
(♪ dramatic music plays)

406
00:21:29,875 --> 00:21:30,875
(music fades)

407
00:21:30,958 --> 00:21:33,083
Bonnie! Time to go to your sleepover.

408
00:21:34,291 --> 00:21:35,250
Hmm.

409
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:38,375
Um…

410
00:21:40,208 --> 00:21:42,666
Yo, Bonnie, uh, what are you doing?

411
00:21:42,750 --> 00:21:44,125
You said you finished packing.

412
00:21:44,208 --> 00:21:47,291
Well, I did, but it's
my very first sleepover, Dad.

413
00:21:47,375 --> 00:21:49,333
I wanna be extra, extra prepared.

414
00:21:49,416 --> 00:21:50,958
You're gonna be fine, sweetie.

415
00:21:51,041 --> 00:21:53,208
Come on. Go put on your shoes.
We got to go.

416
00:21:53,291 --> 00:21:54,291
Okay, okay.

417
00:21:58,958 --> 00:21:59,958
(clears throat)

418
00:22:00,041 --> 00:22:01,125
Jessie. (gasps)

419
00:22:02,791 --> 00:22:03,833
(Lilypad) Uh…

420
00:22:04,375 --> 00:22:05,958
What are you doing?

421
00:22:06,041 --> 00:22:09,500
We are gonna check out
these "friends" for ourselves

422
00:22:09,583 --> 00:22:11,875
and see if there is a real one
in the bunch.

423
00:22:11,958 --> 00:22:13,833
Okay, pause. It is not
a good look for Bonnie

424
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:15,833
- to bring toys to a sleepover.
- (scoffs)

425
00:22:15,916 --> 00:22:17,041
- I do. I do. I do.
- Deputy Buzz.

426
00:22:17,125 --> 00:22:19,541
I do! I mean, I've done things.

427
00:22:19,625 --> 00:22:21,500
Make sure that device
don't take charge of anything

428
00:22:21,583 --> 00:22:22,458
while we're away.

429
00:22:22,541 --> 00:22:23,625
Yes, Sheriff. I'm on it.

430
00:22:23,708 --> 00:22:25,541
- (Dad) All right, time to go.
- (Bonnie) Okay.

431
00:22:26,083 --> 00:22:27,625
No, Jessie. Get out of that bag.

432
00:22:27,708 --> 00:22:29,833
I'm only thinking about
what's best for Bonnie.

433
00:22:29,916 --> 00:22:32,750
Well, what do you know?
That's exactly what I'm doing.

434
00:22:38,625 --> 00:22:40,375
- (door closes)
- (car rumbling)

435
00:22:41,041 --> 00:22:42,541
(Dad) Did you pack your toothbrush?

436
00:22:42,625 --> 00:22:44,125
- (Bonnie) I think so.
- (zipper opens)

437
00:22:45,666 --> 00:22:48,708
Oh, thanks, Dad. You packed
Jessie and Bullseye.

438
00:22:48,791 --> 00:22:51,416
Uh, did I? Well, you're welcome.

439
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:52,708
(Bonnie sighs)

440
00:22:52,791 --> 00:22:54,708
- And here we are.
- (gasps)

441
00:22:55,291 --> 00:22:56,458
Oh, oh, oh, oh!

442
00:22:56,958 --> 00:22:59,250
I wonder if Kara and Heidi are here yet.

443
00:22:59,791 --> 00:23:02,416
Oh! Over there. Dad,
I see them. Park right there.

444
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:04,333
(Dad) Okay, okay. I see them.

445
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:08,041
Uh, Bonnie. You forgot your bag.

446
00:23:08,125 --> 00:23:09,250
(panting)

447
00:23:09,333 --> 00:23:11,625
- Hey, Chelsea.
- Oh, hey, Bonnie.

448
00:23:11,708 --> 00:23:13,833
- Guys, you remember Bonnie?
- Hi.

449
00:23:13,916 --> 00:23:15,666
And this is Jessie.

450
00:23:15,750 --> 00:23:18,291
(as Jessie) I ain't afraid
of nothin', partner.

451
00:23:19,833 --> 00:23:22,625
Oh. You still play with toys?

452
00:23:22,708 --> 00:23:25,083
(friends laughing)

453
00:23:25,166 --> 00:23:26,166
(Bonnie gasps)

454
00:23:26,791 --> 00:23:28,875
Um… Uh…

455
00:23:30,208 --> 00:23:32,166
Uh, um… uh…

456
00:23:32,250 --> 00:23:33,625
No. Be right back.

457
00:23:34,791 --> 00:23:36,291
- Here you go, sweetie.
- Dad, take these.

458
00:23:36,375 --> 00:23:37,750
But I thought you wanted your toys?

459
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:38,958
Dad, just go.

460
00:23:42,041 --> 00:23:43,541
(♪ ominous music plays)

461
00:23:43,625 --> 00:23:44,625
(gasps)

462
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:47,958
Guys,

463
00:23:48,041 --> 00:23:49,833
- I got my Lilypad.
- Bye!

464
00:23:49,916 --> 00:23:51,666
- (gasps)
- (Bonnie groans)

465
00:23:53,208 --> 00:23:54,208
No.

466
00:23:55,416 --> 00:23:56,708
(Bonnie grunts)

467
00:24:03,333 --> 00:24:04,500
(grunts)

468
00:24:05,333 --> 00:24:07,083
(panting)

469
00:24:09,458 --> 00:24:10,625
(groans)

470
00:24:11,916 --> 00:24:12,916
(grunts)

471
00:24:18,250 --> 00:24:19,500
(gasps)

472
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:20,416
No, no, no.

473
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:24,125
No, no, no, this is all wrong.

474
00:24:24,208 --> 00:24:25,583
How is she supposed to make friends

475
00:24:25,666 --> 00:24:27,250
if they ain't even looking at each oth--

476
00:24:27,333 --> 00:24:28,333
(screams)

477
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:30,625
Oh.

478
00:24:30,708 --> 00:24:32,458
- (gasps)
- (footsteps approaching)

479
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:38,083
Oh, no. Somebody lost their toys.

480
00:24:38,166 --> 00:24:39,000
What's that?

481
00:24:39,083 --> 00:24:41,750
I said somebody lost their toys.

482
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,291
Let's see.

483
00:24:45,375 --> 00:24:46,375
(gasps)

484
00:24:46,458 --> 00:24:49,333
They belong to an Emily.

485
00:24:49,416 --> 00:24:51,708
(driver) Oh, and there's an address.

486
00:24:51,791 --> 00:24:53,833
- That's not too far from here.
- (gasps)

487
00:24:53,916 --> 00:24:55,541
We can drop them off.

488
00:25:04,125 --> 00:25:06,291
(phone) <i>Turn right onto Ranch Road.</i>

489
00:25:13,458 --> 00:25:15,083
(phone) <i>You've reached your destination.</i>

490
00:25:15,166 --> 00:25:16,333
(grunting)

491
00:25:16,416 --> 00:25:18,375
I'll just leave them here in the mailbox.

492
00:25:18,458 --> 00:25:19,291
What's that?

493
00:25:19,375 --> 00:25:20,833
I'm leaving them in the mailbox.

494
00:25:20,916 --> 00:25:22,541
- You're leaving me?
- Yes.

495
00:25:22,625 --> 00:25:24,458
(panting) No, no, no.

496
00:25:24,541 --> 00:25:25,875
No, no, no.

497
00:25:27,625 --> 00:25:29,750
No! (panting)

498
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:31,666
We cannot be here.

499
00:25:31,750 --> 00:25:35,166
We've gotta get back to Bonnie!

500
00:25:35,250 --> 00:25:36,583
Come on, Bullseye. (grunts)

501
00:25:36,666 --> 00:25:38,666
(♪ adventurous music playing)

502
00:25:39,416 --> 00:25:40,541
(Jessie panting)

503
00:25:41,916 --> 00:25:43,083
(exclaims, grunts)

504
00:25:45,833 --> 00:25:47,833
(♪ ominous music playing)

505
00:25:50,916 --> 00:25:53,000
- (gasps)
- (grunts)

506
00:25:54,916 --> 00:25:56,250
(thuds)

507
00:25:56,916 --> 00:25:58,750
- (snorts)
- (Jessie shouts)

508
00:25:58,833 --> 00:25:59,750
(screams)

509
00:26:00,250 --> 00:26:01,916
Uh-oh! Uh! Oh!

510
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,625
(chuckling) Whoa!

511
00:26:04,708 --> 00:26:05,916
Whoo!

512
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:08,166
(laughing)

513
00:26:09,125 --> 00:26:10,333
Hi!

514
00:26:10,416 --> 00:26:13,041
Bullseye! You thinking what I'm thinking?

515
00:26:13,666 --> 00:26:16,041
Yeah! Yeah, I'm gonna speak critter,

516
00:26:16,125 --> 00:26:18,125
and we'll ride this horse home!

517
00:26:18,208 --> 00:26:19,916
We're coming, Bonnie!

518
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,458
Yeehaw!

519
00:26:22,541 --> 00:26:24,458
- (whinnies)
- (Jessie shouts)

520
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:27,208
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Wrong way, horsey!

521
00:26:27,291 --> 00:26:29,208
Wrong way!

522
00:26:29,291 --> 00:26:32,541
- (whinnies)
- Whoa, horsey! Whoa!

523
00:26:33,875 --> 00:26:36,500
No! No, no, no, no!

524
00:26:36,583 --> 00:26:39,250
- Whoa!
- (thudding)

525
00:26:42,916 --> 00:26:45,250
(Jessie coughing)

526
00:26:46,208 --> 00:26:47,458
(groans)

527
00:26:47,541 --> 00:26:49,875
(coughs, groans)

528
00:26:49,958 --> 00:26:51,041
(sighs)

529
00:26:51,583 --> 00:26:52,625
Bullseye?

530
00:26:52,708 --> 00:26:54,500
(horse whinnies, snorts)

531
00:26:55,458 --> 00:26:56,333
(Jessie) Oh!

532
00:26:56,416 --> 00:26:58,333
Thank goodness. Come here. Help me.

533
00:26:59,375 --> 00:27:00,500
(person) Daffodil?

534
00:27:02,916 --> 00:27:04,208
Geez, are you all right?

535
00:27:04,291 --> 00:27:06,208
- (gasps)
- Did something spook you?

536
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:08,666
Come on, girl. (clicks tongue)

537
00:27:08,750 --> 00:27:11,125
Come on. Good girl.

538
00:27:13,708 --> 00:27:14,708
Hmm?

539
00:27:15,208 --> 00:27:16,208
(gasps)

540
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,458
Where'd you come from?

541
00:27:19,666 --> 00:27:21,291
(chuckling) He's perfect.

542
00:27:22,750 --> 00:27:25,416
No. Bullseye.

543
00:27:30,125 --> 00:27:32,583
Mmm… Hmm.

544
00:27:32,666 --> 00:27:33,666
Hmm.

545
00:27:33,750 --> 00:27:36,375
And how exactly will this help
us get Bonnie's attention?

546
00:27:36,458 --> 00:27:38,750
Well, when they come back
from the sleepover…

547
00:27:38,833 --> 00:27:40,416
- Careful. That tickles.
- …she'll enter the room,

548
00:27:40,500 --> 00:27:43,875
see Forky and Karen Beverly,
and remember the wedding.

549
00:27:43,958 --> 00:27:46,000
We are talking about Bonnie, right?

550
00:27:46,083 --> 00:27:47,291
And not Jessie?

551
00:27:47,375 --> 00:27:48,375
Huh? (chuckles)

552
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:51,208
Of course Bonnie. (chuckles) Just Bonnie.

553
00:27:51,291 --> 00:27:52,833
Hey, what's everyone talking about?

554
00:27:52,916 --> 00:27:54,750
Buzz is gonna propose to Jessie.

555
00:27:54,833 --> 00:27:56,291
- Propose?
- (Trixie) Finally.

556
00:27:56,375 --> 00:27:57,875
Wait a minute. Wait…
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

557
00:27:57,958 --> 00:27:59,416
(stammers) I didn't say that.

558
00:27:59,500 --> 00:28:00,916
- You didn't not say it either.
- Well, I…

559
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:01,875
Who, Buzz?

560
00:28:01,958 --> 00:28:04,291
Question. Is Woody gonna
perform the wedding ceremony?

561
00:28:04,375 --> 00:28:07,083
I haven't thought
that far in advance, Forky.

562
00:28:07,166 --> 00:28:08,916
Okay. Then why is Woody at the window?

563
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:10,750
(all gasp) Woody!

564
00:28:11,583 --> 00:28:12,583
Woody!

565
00:28:12,666 --> 00:28:14,166
- Hey, everybody!
- (all) Bo!

566
00:28:14,250 --> 00:28:16,041
Howdy, folks. Coast clear?

567
00:28:16,125 --> 00:28:17,375
The stage is yours, my friend.

568
00:28:17,458 --> 00:28:18,750
(all) Woody!

569
00:28:18,833 --> 00:28:20,791
- It's good to s…
- Wow.

570
00:28:20,875 --> 00:28:22,750
(♪ Western guitar plays)

571
00:28:22,833 --> 00:28:24,625
Pretty cowboy.

572
00:28:24,708 --> 00:28:26,125
Why are you wearing a dress, Woody?

573
00:28:26,208 --> 00:28:28,291
It's called a poncho, Forky.

574
00:28:28,375 --> 00:28:29,958
Thought I'd change it up.

575
00:28:30,041 --> 00:28:31,041
Yeah?

576
00:28:33,375 --> 00:28:34,625
Well, Bo likes it.

577
00:28:35,375 --> 00:28:37,666
(sighs) It's good to be back.

578
00:28:38,375 --> 00:28:39,666
- Shiny.
- What?

579
00:28:39,750 --> 00:28:41,250
- (all) Nothing.
- Love the poncho.

580
00:28:41,333 --> 00:28:42,666
Someone needs a brown marker.

581
00:28:42,750 --> 00:28:45,041
Wow. Look what Bonnie's done
with the place.

582
00:28:45,125 --> 00:28:48,000
(chuckling) It's…
She really let things go.

583
00:28:48,083 --> 00:28:49,000
- Oh, my.
- Oh.

584
00:28:49,083 --> 00:28:50,541
I see Sammy got bigger.

585
00:28:51,041 --> 00:28:54,458
- Uh, that's Sammy number two.
- No.

586
00:28:54,541 --> 00:28:56,041
- (all) Yeah.
- I'll explain it.

587
00:28:56,125 --> 00:28:58,625
There was a Sammy number one,
and then he died.

588
00:28:58,708 --> 00:28:59,916
- Poor Samuel.
- (beeping)

589
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:02,083
- Halt. Who goes there?
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

590
00:29:02,166 --> 00:29:05,000
Sor… Sorry. My name is Woody.

591
00:29:05,083 --> 00:29:07,375
I come in peace. Used to live here.

592
00:29:07,458 --> 00:29:08,458
All right.

593
00:29:08,541 --> 00:29:09,541
(chuckles)

594
00:29:09,625 --> 00:29:11,458
It's been too long, cowboy.

595
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:13,916
- How've you been?
- Ah, busy.

596
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,625
Came here as fast as I could
after Jessie called for help.

597
00:29:16,708 --> 00:29:18,583
- Good thing we were in town.
- She called you?

598
00:29:19,083 --> 00:29:20,916
- Yeah, I'm her deputy.
- But I'm her deputy.

599
00:29:21,625 --> 00:29:23,250
- Uh…
- (chuckles)

600
00:29:23,333 --> 00:29:24,958
- That's odd.
- (chuckling) Well, well…

601
00:29:25,041 --> 00:29:26,333
there must be a little mix-up here.

602
00:29:26,416 --> 00:29:28,625
- Well, no offense, Woody.
- Oh, none taken. None taken.

603
00:29:28,708 --> 00:29:29,666
But she literally

604
00:29:29,750 --> 00:29:31,500
- deputized me.
- Oh, is that so?

605
00:29:31,583 --> 00:29:33,125
- Woody, look. Eyes here.
- Uh-huh.

606
00:29:33,208 --> 00:29:35,375
- Star. Deputy. Me.
- Uh-huh.

607
00:29:35,458 --> 00:29:37,333
- No star.
- (stammers) I got you.

608
00:29:37,416 --> 00:29:38,791
Star. No star.

609
00:29:38,875 --> 00:29:41,291
- Oh, hey, Buzz, what is that?
- What? Where?

610
00:29:41,791 --> 00:29:42,625
Ow.

611
00:29:42,708 --> 00:29:43,791
- Hey. Wait…
- What?

612
00:29:43,875 --> 00:29:45,708
Just happy to help, Deputy.

613
00:29:45,791 --> 00:29:49,250
(sighs) Call me when
you're done helping, dear.

614
00:29:49,333 --> 00:29:50,375
(Woody) Thanks, Bo.

615
00:29:50,458 --> 00:29:51,833
(Duke) Okay, ladies.

616
00:29:51,916 --> 00:29:53,541
- (Bo) Girls weekend!
- Yes.

617
00:29:53,625 --> 00:29:55,416
<i>Un, deux, trois!</i>

618
00:29:55,500 --> 00:29:56,375
(horn beeps)

619
00:29:57,708 --> 00:29:59,000
Where is Jessie, anyway?

620
00:29:59,083 --> 00:30:00,250
Sleepover reconnaissance.

621
00:30:00,333 --> 00:30:02,541
Yeah, she and Bullseye are
helping Bonnie make friends.

622
00:30:02,625 --> 00:30:05,208
While fending off the nefarious Lilypad.

623
00:30:05,291 --> 00:30:07,708
It's Dolly, by the way. Glasses.

624
00:30:07,791 --> 00:30:09,166
Didn't you always have glasses?

625
00:30:09,250 --> 00:30:10,458
What? No.

626
00:30:10,541 --> 00:30:12,666
We've got it handled, cowboy.

627
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:13,958
As her deputy, I'm certain

628
00:30:14,041 --> 00:30:16,541
Jessie's resting
on a comfy pillow right now

629
00:30:16,625 --> 00:30:18,791
making all the difference for Bonnie.

630
00:30:18,875 --> 00:30:21,083
(Jessie groaning, straining)

631
00:30:24,458 --> 00:30:25,875
(groaning continues)

632
00:30:25,958 --> 00:30:26,833
(sighs)

633
00:30:26,916 --> 00:30:28,000
(whinnies)

634
00:30:28,583 --> 00:30:30,500
(scoffs) You're no help.

635
00:30:30,583 --> 00:30:31,416
(gasps)

636
00:30:31,500 --> 00:30:33,416
Hey, you can help get me out of here.

637
00:30:33,500 --> 00:30:34,416
(summons Daffodil)

638
00:30:34,500 --> 00:30:36,958
Come here. Come on. Come on. Daffodil.

639
00:30:37,041 --> 00:30:38,500
Yeah, yeah, come over here.

640
00:30:38,583 --> 00:30:39,750
Come on. Come on.

641
00:30:39,833 --> 00:30:40,833
(gasps)

642
00:30:40,916 --> 00:30:42,666
- (snorts)
- (chuckles)

643
00:30:42,750 --> 00:30:44,791
Nice pig. Nice pig.

644
00:30:44,875 --> 00:30:46,416
Stinky pig.

645
00:30:46,500 --> 00:30:48,375
- (screams)
- (grunts)

646
00:30:48,458 --> 00:30:50,000
Hey, hey, there.

647
00:30:50,083 --> 00:30:51,666
(stammers) I guess you'll have to do.

648
00:30:52,208 --> 00:30:54,625
Jimmy Dean?

649
00:30:54,708 --> 00:30:56,791
You mean, like, the… Oh, no.

650
00:30:56,875 --> 00:30:57,833
- (squeals)
- Oh!

651
00:30:57,916 --> 00:30:59,666
- Okay. Wow, that's your name?
- (grunting)

652
00:30:59,750 --> 00:31:00,750
Jimmy Dean?

653
00:31:00,833 --> 00:31:03,333
Take me to the house.

654
00:31:03,416 --> 00:31:04,750
- (squealing)
- (gasps)

655
00:31:04,833 --> 00:31:07,208
Golly gee whillikers! It's working.

656
00:31:07,291 --> 00:31:08,833
(exclaiming)

657
00:31:08,916 --> 00:31:10,458
Hey! Ugh! Yuck!

658
00:31:10,541 --> 00:31:13,041
(gasping) Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

659
00:31:13,583 --> 00:31:14,458
Yes!

660
00:31:14,541 --> 00:31:18,250
Yes. Yes, good pig. Good pig. Good--

661
00:31:18,333 --> 00:31:20,208
No. No, no, no.

662
00:31:20,291 --> 00:31:22,250
Bad pig. Oh, wrong way, Jimmy.

663
00:31:22,333 --> 00:31:25,041
Oh, no, no. Wrong house, Jimmy.

664
00:31:25,125 --> 00:31:26,375
Wrong house. Wrong-- (grunts)

665
00:31:27,041 --> 00:31:28,583
(Jimmy grunting)

666
00:31:28,666 --> 00:31:29,666
No. (grunts)

667
00:31:29,750 --> 00:31:31,833
(panting, strains)

668
00:31:32,375 --> 00:31:33,833
- (Combat Carl) Blaze?
- (gasps)

669
00:31:34,333 --> 00:31:35,458
(all groan)

670
00:31:35,541 --> 00:31:36,833
False alarm, everyone.

671
00:31:37,333 --> 00:31:38,416
Um…

672
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:41,375
Oh, apologies. Where are
Combat Carl's manners?

673
00:31:41,458 --> 00:31:43,333
(stammers) Welcome. Please, take a seat.

674
00:31:43,416 --> 00:31:44,416
Oh. (chuckles)

675
00:31:44,500 --> 00:31:46,791
No. I've gotta get home.

676
00:31:46,875 --> 00:31:47,791
- No, no! Sit.
- Please, sit.

677
00:31:47,875 --> 00:31:49,750
- (speaks Spanish)
- Combat Carl insists.

678
00:31:49,833 --> 00:31:51,583
Oh. Okay.

679
00:31:51,666 --> 00:31:53,000
- (all clamoring)
- No, no, no!

680
00:31:53,083 --> 00:31:55,500
- Oh, sorry. I'm sorry.
- Any chair but that one.

681
00:31:56,041 --> 00:31:57,250
Who… Who sits there?

682
00:31:57,333 --> 00:31:58,500
(all) Blaze.

683
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:01,500
Blaze. You mean the girl I saw
in the barn?

684
00:32:01,583 --> 00:32:02,541
She's your kid?

685
00:32:02,625 --> 00:32:04,750
(sighs) Isn't she swell?

686
00:32:04,833 --> 00:32:06,208
She loves her tea parties.

687
00:32:06,291 --> 00:32:08,750
And telling us all her secrets.

688
00:32:08,833 --> 00:32:10,791
That's right, Pizza With Sunglasses.

689
00:32:10,875 --> 00:32:12,041
To Blaze's return.

690
00:32:12,125 --> 00:32:13,833
(all) To Blaze's return!

691
00:32:13,916 --> 00:32:16,000
(sipping)

692
00:32:16,625 --> 00:32:17,916
Mmm. <i>Rico.</i>

693
00:32:18,458 --> 00:32:19,625
Ooh, hot.

694
00:32:19,708 --> 00:32:21,208
(smacks lips) Uh…

695
00:32:21,291 --> 00:32:26,083
How long has it been
since your Blaze last had tea?

696
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,708
Things were never really the same

697
00:32:29,791 --> 00:32:31,708
- once he arrived.
- He?

698
00:32:31,791 --> 00:32:34,666
Smarty Pants. Blaze's first device.

699
00:32:34,750 --> 00:32:36,500
- You're sitting on him.
- What?

700
00:32:36,583 --> 00:32:38,750
(gasps) Holy butterscotch!

701
00:32:38,833 --> 00:32:39,666
(beeps)

702
00:32:39,750 --> 00:32:41,375
(♪ playing music)

703
00:32:41,458 --> 00:32:43,291
<i>Why, hello there. Pick a number.</i>

704
00:32:43,375 --> 00:32:44,583
- Not again!
- Make it stop! Don't!

705
00:32:45,375 --> 00:32:47,416
- Oh, just kill me.
- Come on.

706
00:32:47,500 --> 00:32:49,000
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

707
00:32:49,083 --> 00:32:50,041
- Hey, hey!
- No! Don't!

708
00:32:50,125 --> 00:32:52,583
This… This isn't the bathroom.

709
00:32:53,333 --> 00:32:54,333
How long have I been off?

710
00:32:54,416 --> 00:32:55,708
- Shut up, chair!
- We hate you.

711
00:32:55,791 --> 00:32:56,791
Turn him off.

712
00:32:56,875 --> 00:32:58,625
(groans) Gosh.

713
00:32:59,708 --> 00:33:03,041
Who's this little, old, tiny grandma lady?

714
00:33:03,125 --> 00:33:06,041
- Gosh, what is wrong with him?
- Low batteries.

715
00:33:06,125 --> 00:33:07,333
(Smarty Pants groaning)

716
00:33:07,416 --> 00:33:08,583
Eggman?

717
00:33:08,666 --> 00:33:10,708
(groans) You're one of those Pond devices.

718
00:33:10,791 --> 00:33:11,708
- (burps)
- (groans)

719
00:33:11,791 --> 00:33:14,166
I already have to put up with
a Lilypad back home.

720
00:33:14,250 --> 00:33:16,083
- Hey.
- I don't have time for this.

721
00:33:16,166 --> 00:33:19,583
(grunting) Your Blaze took my
horse into the house…

722
00:33:20,458 --> 00:33:22,958
and we gotta get back to our own kid.

723
00:33:23,041 --> 00:33:25,541
Wait, wait, wait, wait.
You're going inside?

724
00:33:25,625 --> 00:33:28,625
- Take me with you, please!
- Not a chance.

725
00:33:28,708 --> 00:33:29,791
You need help pushing?

726
00:33:29,875 --> 00:33:31,583
I'm… (hiccups) …great with pushing.

727
00:33:32,375 --> 00:33:34,458
<i>You can do it. You can do it.</i>
<i>Like a choo-choo,</i>

728
00:33:34,541 --> 00:33:35,375
<i>- you can poop.</i>
<i>- </i>No!

729
00:33:35,458 --> 00:33:37,791
How about you just wait here
with your friends?

730
00:33:37,875 --> 00:33:41,000
Spend another second with
Corporal No-Pants? (hiccups)

731
00:33:41,083 --> 00:33:42,250
I'm coming with you, cowgirl.

732
00:33:42,333 --> 00:33:44,791
No way. Your kind's caused me
enough trouble.

733
00:33:44,875 --> 00:33:46,166
My kind?

734
00:33:46,250 --> 00:33:47,833
- Take him!
- Please! Get him out of here!

735
00:33:47,916 --> 00:33:49,250
All he's good for is chair.

736
00:33:49,333 --> 00:33:52,041
I am not a chair!

737
00:33:52,541 --> 00:33:55,833
I am a potty trainer!

738
00:33:55,916 --> 00:33:58,041
Show some respect!

739
00:33:58,583 --> 00:34:01,791
Okay, listen, Raggedy Ann.
All these losers are outdoor toys.

740
00:34:01,875 --> 00:34:04,500
I'm the only one who's
done time inside. (hiccups)

741
00:34:04,583 --> 00:34:06,458
You wanna find your horsey? Clippity-clop.

742
00:34:06,541 --> 00:34:09,041
I know exactly where Blaze put him, okay?

743
00:34:09,125 --> 00:34:11,000
You need me. You need me. You need me.

744
00:34:11,083 --> 00:34:13,041
You need me. You need me. You need me.

745
00:34:14,708 --> 00:34:15,875
Hi.

746
00:34:16,708 --> 00:34:18,833
(Jessie) Move. Move.

747
00:34:19,333 --> 00:34:20,166
(all grunt)

748
00:34:22,375 --> 00:34:24,625
Hey, geez. Someone dim
the brightness out here.

749
00:34:24,708 --> 00:34:25,833
- Shut up.
- Would you try walking

750
00:34:25,916 --> 00:34:27,291
- a little less bouncy?
- Shut up.

751
00:34:27,375 --> 00:34:29,500
Quick. Lock the door before
they change their minds.

752
00:34:29,583 --> 00:34:30,583
Copy that.

753
00:34:32,708 --> 00:34:35,291
(♪ marching music playing)

754
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:46,500
(gasps) Halt.

755
00:34:50,541 --> 00:34:52,500
(wailing sound playing)

756
00:34:56,708 --> 00:34:58,333
(sniffing)

757
00:35:00,416 --> 00:35:01,416
(wailing stops)

758
00:35:04,291 --> 00:35:05,791
- (sniffs)
- (chuckles)

759
00:35:06,625 --> 00:35:11,166
♪ <i>Love is a song</i>
<i>That never ends</i> ♪

760
00:35:11,250 --> 00:35:12,250
(Buzzes chuckle)

761
00:35:12,333 --> 00:35:15,208
♪ <i>Life may be swift</i>
<i>And fleeting</i> ♪

762
00:35:15,291 --> 00:35:17,708
(all chuckling)

763
00:35:18,416 --> 00:35:23,500
♪ <i>Hope may die</i>
<i>Yet love's beautiful music</i> ♪

764
00:35:23,583 --> 00:35:27,333
♪ <i>Comes each day</i>
<i>Like the dawn--</i> ♪

765
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:29,416
(♪ ominous music playing)

766
00:35:30,708 --> 00:35:32,791
Hon, I'm pretty sure we go this way.

767
00:35:33,708 --> 00:35:34,833
(spouse) You sure?

768
00:35:34,916 --> 00:35:37,166
(grunting)

769
00:35:37,250 --> 00:35:38,708
(footsteps approaching)

770
00:35:38,791 --> 00:35:39,791
Save yourselves.

771
00:35:44,541 --> 00:35:46,875
It's this line here.

772
00:35:46,958 --> 00:35:49,000
If we follow it…

773
00:35:49,083 --> 00:35:50,750
- There's our camp.
- Oh, I see.

774
00:35:50,833 --> 00:35:52,083
Yeah, that looks right.

775
00:35:53,583 --> 00:35:55,333
Hey, wait for me, guys!

776
00:35:57,166 --> 00:35:59,625
- Whoa. No way.
- (all gasp)

777
00:35:59,708 --> 00:36:01,791
Hey, Morgan! Look at this.

778
00:36:01,875 --> 00:36:03,541
(Morgan) Lucky. Hey, let me see it.

779
00:36:03,625 --> 00:36:04,625
Nope. Finders keepers.

780
00:36:04,708 --> 00:36:05,541
- Mom!
- Man down.

781
00:36:05,625 --> 00:36:06,625
- Code red.
- Code red.

782
00:36:06,708 --> 00:36:08,791
- Code red. Code red. Code red.
- Kids, be nice.

783
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:11,666
Code red. Code red. Code red.

784
00:36:14,083 --> 00:36:16,875
Blaze, I'm going out. Be back in an hour.

785
00:36:16,958 --> 00:36:18,208
(Blaze) Okay, Mom.

786
00:36:22,083 --> 00:36:24,166
(grunts, panting)

787
00:36:24,250 --> 00:36:26,166
Get Bullseye, get out.
Get Bullseye, get out.

788
00:36:26,250 --> 00:36:27,958
- Hey, cowgirl?
- Shh.

789
00:36:28,541 --> 00:36:30,791
- (gasps)
- Ooh. Forgot my keys.

790
00:36:32,916 --> 00:36:34,333
(Jessie gasps, exclaims)

791
00:36:34,416 --> 00:36:37,416
- Ugh! (coughing)
- (Smarty Pants groaning)

792
00:36:37,500 --> 00:36:38,708
Really don't feel so good.

793
00:36:38,791 --> 00:36:40,916
I think I'm gonna… (burps) …reboot.

794
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:42,000
(♪ upbeat music playing)

795
00:36:42,083 --> 00:36:44,541
Shh. Quiet, quiet, quiet.
Quiet, quiet, quiet, quiet.

796
00:36:44,625 --> 00:36:46,375
- (grunts) Quiet.
- (♪ music stops)

797
00:36:48,333 --> 00:36:49,166
(gasps)

798
00:36:51,708 --> 00:36:53,833
(Smarty Pants) Wait. Wait.

799
00:36:53,916 --> 00:36:55,791
Wait, I'm back.

800
00:36:55,875 --> 00:36:57,583
I'm back home.

801
00:36:58,166 --> 00:37:02,041
- This is where it all started.
- (groans)

802
00:37:02,125 --> 00:37:03,125
Yeah.

803
00:37:03,208 --> 00:37:05,375
- It's all changed.
- (groans)

804
00:37:05,458 --> 00:37:07,500
(gasps) Smarty, no.

805
00:37:07,583 --> 00:37:09,875
I-I have to find Bullseye. Wake up!

806
00:37:09,958 --> 00:37:12,750
- Need more juice.
- (beeping)

807
00:37:12,833 --> 00:37:14,791
Okay! W-Where are the batteries?

808
00:37:14,875 --> 00:37:16,375
Where do I find the batteries?

809
00:37:16,458 --> 00:37:20,916
Bottom drawer, next to the stamps.

810
00:37:22,666 --> 00:37:23,791
(strains)

811
00:37:29,250 --> 00:37:30,958
<i>Why, hello there! Pick a number.</i>

812
00:37:31,041 --> 00:37:31,958
<i>Is it number one?</i>

813
00:37:32,041 --> 00:37:34,375
- Whoa! I feel great!
- Shh!

814
00:37:34,458 --> 00:37:35,708
- Look at me!
- Shh! No!

815
00:37:35,791 --> 00:37:37,791
- Yes! (laughs)
- No, we're not doing this now.

816
00:37:37,875 --> 00:37:38,875
- Not now.
- I am back!

817
00:37:38,958 --> 00:37:41,041
- Cut it out!
- (gasps)

818
00:37:41,125 --> 00:37:43,875
Snappy. Atlas. They're still here!

819
00:37:43,958 --> 00:37:45,916
Oh! Bossy cowgirl,
we have to turn 'em back on.

820
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,291
No! No way.

821
00:37:47,375 --> 00:37:49,375
The last thing this world
needs is more devices.

822
00:37:49,458 --> 00:37:50,583
What, what, what?

823
00:37:50,666 --> 00:37:53,041
You're just gonna shove 'em
back in the dark forever?

824
00:37:53,125 --> 00:37:55,125
Do you have any idea what that's like?

825
00:37:55,208 --> 00:37:56,208
(♪ pensive music playing)

826
00:37:56,291 --> 00:37:57,333
(sighs)

827
00:37:57,416 --> 00:38:00,291
Fine. We gotta make this quick.

828
00:38:00,375 --> 00:38:01,833
(laughs) Yes!

829
00:38:01,916 --> 00:38:04,083
<i>Number one! You made number--</i>

830
00:38:08,375 --> 00:38:09,958
- Atlas! Snappy!
- Smarty!

831
00:38:10,041 --> 00:38:11,750
- Smarty? Is that you?
- Is it really you?

832
00:38:11,833 --> 00:38:14,125
- It's really me! Yes!
- My goodness. You look great.

833
00:38:14,208 --> 00:38:15,833
- The AA-Team is back!
- Oh, my gosh. Yes!

834
00:38:15,916 --> 00:38:17,875
Mom brought us inside
after that tantrum Blaze had,

835
00:38:17,958 --> 00:38:19,000
and we never saw you again.

836
00:38:19,083 --> 00:38:21,041
- So tell me. What did I miss?
- Oh, my gosh.

837
00:38:21,125 --> 00:38:23,208
Well, we've been down a long time too.

838
00:38:23,291 --> 00:38:26,041
But look! I could show you how
first and second grade went!

839
00:38:26,125 --> 00:38:27,333
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Please do that. Yeah.

840
00:38:27,416 --> 00:38:29,625
Look at her! She's so much older.

841
00:38:29,708 --> 00:38:31,250
- I know, right?
- She's adorable.

842
00:38:31,333 --> 00:38:32,916
- Isn't she?
- She got bangs that year.

843
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:35,333
- Wait a minute. Where is that?
- That's Disneyland.

844
00:38:35,416 --> 00:38:36,458
Zoom in. That's me in her pocket.

845
00:38:36,541 --> 00:38:37,916
Oh, flush. You both went there?

846
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:39,541
- (Snappy) Mm-hmm. For reals.
- (Atlas) It's so beautiful.

847
00:38:40,458 --> 00:38:42,291
And, uh, that's the last of it.

848
00:38:42,375 --> 00:38:44,541
Next, it was just
a spinning rainbow wheel.

849
00:38:44,625 --> 00:38:46,083
Then… darkness.

850
00:38:46,166 --> 00:38:48,000
My entire SD card flashed before my eyes.

851
00:38:48,083 --> 00:38:49,166
- (Smarty Pants) Wow.
- (Atlas) Aw.

852
00:38:49,250 --> 00:38:52,750
Okay, okay. I am glad you're
all powered up and stuff,

853
00:38:52,833 --> 00:38:54,750
but we're wasting time I don't got.

854
00:38:54,833 --> 00:38:57,125
Oh, we're so grateful to you, cowboy lady.

855
00:38:57,208 --> 00:38:59,041
Guys, guys, guys,
this is pushy cowgirl Jessie.

856
00:38:59,125 --> 00:39:01,208
She claims she's a sheriff.
Just go with it.

857
00:39:01,291 --> 00:39:03,333
- Blaze has her horse, Banzai--
- Bullseye!

858
00:39:03,416 --> 00:39:05,791
And I gotta get us back
to our kid, Bonnie, now.

859
00:39:05,875 --> 00:39:08,083
She needs us. So, where is he, Smarty?

860
00:39:08,166 --> 00:39:10,833
All right, okay. I said
I'd tell ya, so I'll tell ya.

861
00:39:10,916 --> 00:39:12,833
- Drumroll please.
- (thudding)

862
00:39:12,916 --> 00:39:15,791
He's probably in the bedroom.

863
00:39:15,875 --> 00:39:18,541
Probably in the bedroom?
I could've guessed that.

864
00:39:18,625 --> 00:39:20,875
- And yet, you did not, Dusty.
- Dusty?

865
00:39:20,958 --> 00:39:23,166
Yeah, you know, like ancient,
elderly, mummified old fart.

866
00:39:23,250 --> 00:39:25,541
Or as I like to call it, number 1.5.

867
00:39:25,625 --> 00:39:26,750
- I missed you, Smarty.
- (chuckles)

868
00:39:26,833 --> 00:39:27,833
You know what?

869
00:39:27,916 --> 00:39:29,208
- I've had enough of your cr--
- Oh, wait!

870
00:39:29,833 --> 00:39:32,208
I just had an idea that could
maybe help you get to Bonnie.

871
00:39:32,291 --> 00:39:34,541
- (sighs) What?
- It's a little technical,

872
00:39:34,625 --> 00:39:35,625
but if the three of us link up--

873
00:39:35,708 --> 00:39:38,958
No, no, I am done
with this techno mumbo jumbo.

874
00:39:39,041 --> 00:39:42,291
No offense, but I'll be fine
getting back on my own.

875
00:39:42,375 --> 00:39:43,625
Offense taken!

876
00:39:48,500 --> 00:39:50,583
You're muted, Dave. You're muted.

877
00:39:50,666 --> 00:39:51,875
Okay. There you go.

878
00:39:51,958 --> 00:39:53,625
(Dave)<i> Only have a bit</i>
<i>of time left. One more time--</i>

879
00:39:53,708 --> 00:39:55,291
(Blaze's dad) You're muted again, Dave.

880
00:39:55,375 --> 00:39:57,416
(Smarty Pants grunting)

881
00:39:57,500 --> 00:39:59,000
Oh, cheese and crackers!

882
00:39:59,083 --> 00:40:00,333
What are you doing? Get back.

883
00:40:00,416 --> 00:40:02,916
You're not the only one
who misses their kid, okay?

884
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,291
- Now help us up.
- (sighs)

885
00:40:04,375 --> 00:40:05,375
(all grunting)

886
00:40:05,458 --> 00:40:07,166
Careful, careful! You're gonna unplug me.

887
00:40:07,250 --> 00:40:09,583
- (door opens)
- Blaze, I'm home.

888
00:40:09,666 --> 00:40:10,583
(Blaze) Hey, Mom!

889
00:40:10,666 --> 00:40:11,958
Back, back, back!

890
00:40:12,708 --> 00:40:14,666
- (toys grunting)
- Hey, Mom?

891
00:40:14,750 --> 00:40:17,083
- Wait a second. Is that…
- Is that big girl Blaze?

892
00:40:17,166 --> 00:40:19,541
- She's changed so much!
- Like overnight.

893
00:40:19,625 --> 00:40:21,333
- Is she here yet?
- (Blaze's mom) Not yet.

894
00:40:21,416 --> 00:40:22,416
Why don't you try messaging her?

895
00:40:22,500 --> 00:40:24,000
- (Snappy) Whoa.
- She big, big.

896
00:40:24,083 --> 00:40:25,833
- She…
- (toilet flushes)

897
00:40:25,916 --> 00:40:28,041
She did it without me.

898
00:40:36,791 --> 00:40:38,041
- (Snappy) Wow.
- (gasps)

899
00:40:38,125 --> 00:40:39,541
- It's so pretty.
- It's so clean!

900
00:40:39,625 --> 00:40:40,833
(Smarty Pants) When did she become neat?

901
00:40:40,916 --> 00:40:42,125
(Atlas) I can see the floor.

902
00:40:42,208 --> 00:40:43,791
(Snappy) I can see me in the floor.

903
00:40:43,875 --> 00:40:45,666
It smells like vanilla.

904
00:40:45,750 --> 00:40:46,791
With hints of brown sugar.

905
00:40:46,875 --> 00:40:48,416
(Smarty Pants) You know who I don't miss?

906
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:49,625
(Snappy) That stupid stuffed whale.

907
00:40:49,708 --> 00:40:51,583
- (Atlas) <i>What was his name?</i>
- (Smarty Pants) <i>Spouty.</i>

908
00:40:51,666 --> 00:40:52,916
(Snappy) <i>The worst.</i>

909
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,208
(Smarty Pants) <i>Give me a break.</i>

910
00:40:54,291 --> 00:40:55,291
(Snappy) <i>Annoying.</i>

911
00:40:55,375 --> 00:40:58,333
Seriously, how much have we missed?

912
00:40:58,416 --> 00:40:59,458
Everything.

913
00:40:59,958 --> 00:41:02,583
Your Blaze ain't the kid
you remember anymore.

914
00:41:02,666 --> 00:41:03,875
How would you know?

915
00:41:03,958 --> 00:41:07,166
(sighs) I've seen all this before.

916
00:41:07,250 --> 00:41:08,875
Spent a lot of years under the bed

917
00:41:08,958 --> 00:41:11,708
watching my first kid grow up without me.

918
00:41:13,833 --> 00:41:15,333
- Hey, that's our address.
- (GPS beeping)

919
00:41:15,416 --> 00:41:17,541
How old is Blaze anyway? Nine, ten?

920
00:41:17,625 --> 00:41:19,041
Her room looks like a teenager's.

921
00:41:19,125 --> 00:41:20,916
She's nine and a half,
thank you very much.

922
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:23,791
It's 'cause you devices
make 'em change so fast.

923
00:41:23,875 --> 00:41:25,541
(groans) I gotta get back.

924
00:41:25,625 --> 00:41:27,583
- So, where--
- (whinnies)

925
00:41:28,208 --> 00:41:30,500
Bullseye! Thank goodness.

926
00:41:31,583 --> 00:41:34,000
Uh-huh, they seem nice, Bullseye,

927
00:41:34,083 --> 00:41:35,291
but we have to go now.

928
00:41:35,375 --> 00:41:36,916
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

929
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:39,291
So you're saying that
this was your room too?

930
00:41:39,375 --> 00:41:41,000
- Yes.
- (scoffs) Really?

931
00:41:41,083 --> 00:41:43,083
- (chuckling)
- What, you calling me a liar?

932
00:41:43,166 --> 00:41:44,166
No…

933
00:41:45,208 --> 00:41:46,791
Yeah. Yeah, liar.

934
00:41:46,875 --> 00:41:48,291
(sighs)

935
00:41:48,375 --> 00:41:49,375
(♪ tense music playing)

936
00:41:49,916 --> 00:41:51,500
There's a knot in the ceiling,

937
00:41:51,583 --> 00:41:53,291
looks like an angry eye
when you squint at it.

938
00:41:53,375 --> 00:41:54,916
Window's got a small crack

939
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:56,625
like a spider in
the upper right-hand corner.

940
00:41:56,708 --> 00:41:58,958
And out on that tire swing hill,

941
00:41:59,041 --> 00:42:01,625
Emily and I would play
every summer afternoon.

942
00:42:01,708 --> 00:42:03,416
Now, Bullseye, let's go.

943
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:05,375
Uh, you're welcome.

944
00:42:05,458 --> 00:42:08,541
For what? You didn't help me
at all. You were--

945
00:42:08,625 --> 00:42:10,958
What? Go on. Say it.

946
00:42:13,291 --> 00:42:15,000
- Useless.
- (gasps)

947
00:42:15,083 --> 00:42:16,583
- Oh, no, she didn't.
- Oh, snap!

948
00:42:16,666 --> 00:42:18,416
- (Jimmy Dean snorting)
- (gasps)

949
00:42:18,500 --> 00:42:20,458
Oh, no. Not the pig!

950
00:42:22,375 --> 00:42:25,333
(♪ "I Love It" playing through headphones)

951
00:42:25,958 --> 00:42:27,666
- (Blaze humming)
- (snorting)

952
00:42:27,750 --> 00:42:28,916
Jimmy got big.

953
00:42:30,291 --> 00:42:31,958
Lay it on me, Jimmy Dean!

954
00:42:32,750 --> 00:42:36,375
Who's coming? Sally's coming.
Who's coming? Sally's coming.

955
00:42:36,458 --> 00:42:40,250
Yeah, yeah. She's coming.
She's coming to my house.

956
00:42:41,166 --> 00:42:43,333
Hey, Mom! Sally's texting me right now.

957
00:42:43,416 --> 00:42:44,750
She's probably on her way.

958
00:42:49,083 --> 00:42:51,083
(♪ melancholy music playing)

959
00:42:54,541 --> 00:42:55,750
(sighs)

960
00:43:02,791 --> 00:43:04,791
(sobbing)

961
00:43:08,583 --> 00:43:10,416
(snorting)

962
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:20,625
You'll be my friend, right, Jimmy?

963
00:43:25,583 --> 00:43:26,958
Always.

964
00:43:27,875 --> 00:43:32,666
By the way, your hair looks so good today.

965
00:43:32,750 --> 00:43:34,041
(chuckles)

966
00:43:34,125 --> 00:43:35,333
Thank you, Jimmy.

967
00:43:38,583 --> 00:43:41,041
She's perfect!

968
00:43:41,125 --> 00:43:42,125
(blusters)

969
00:43:42,208 --> 00:43:44,541
We gotta get Blaze to meet Bonnie.

970
00:43:44,625 --> 00:43:45,958
(chuckles)

971
00:43:46,041 --> 00:43:47,500
(snoring)

972
00:43:47,583 --> 00:43:48,583
- Bonnie.
- (gasps)

973
00:43:48,666 --> 00:43:49,708
Tag, you're it!

974
00:43:49,791 --> 00:43:50,791
We're home.

975
00:43:50,875 --> 00:43:52,958
Hi, hon. How was the sleepover?

976
00:43:53,041 --> 00:43:54,250
I don't wanna talk about it.

977
00:43:54,333 --> 00:43:56,416
- Why? What happened?
- Nothing.

978
00:43:56,500 --> 00:43:57,666
That doesn't sound good.

979
00:43:57,750 --> 00:43:59,166
I don't see Jessie.

980
00:43:59,250 --> 00:44:00,291
Calm down, lover boy.

981
00:44:00,375 --> 00:44:01,500
Your fiancée's coming.

982
00:44:01,583 --> 00:44:02,833
Fiancée?

983
00:44:02,916 --> 00:44:05,208
Buzz Lightyear, you never told me.

984
00:44:05,291 --> 00:44:08,416
I know. Isn't it exciting?
Well, it's not official yet.

985
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:10,166
I have to, you know, ask her.

986
00:44:10,250 --> 00:44:12,250
Uh, FYI, I am ordained.

987
00:44:12,333 --> 00:44:14,041
- Since when?
- Last Halloween.

988
00:44:14,125 --> 00:44:15,833
Bonnie made me a haunted priest, remember?

989
00:44:15,916 --> 00:44:17,166
- (toys) Oh, yeah.
- Guys, places.

990
00:44:17,250 --> 00:44:18,250
Bonnie's coming.

991
00:44:20,541 --> 00:44:21,916
(Bonnie's mom) Did you make some friends?

992
00:44:22,000 --> 00:44:23,000
I guess so.

993
00:44:23,083 --> 00:44:24,583
Aw, she looks awful.

994
00:44:24,666 --> 00:44:25,833
Does anyone see Jessie?

995
00:44:26,916 --> 00:44:28,416
(Woody) So, that's Lilypad?

996
00:44:28,500 --> 00:44:30,208
(Bonnie's mom)
How about I make you a snack?

997
00:44:30,291 --> 00:44:32,583
(Bonnie) Yes, please. I'm starving.

998
00:44:32,666 --> 00:44:35,375
Jessie. (grunts) Jessie. Bullseye.

999
00:44:35,458 --> 00:44:36,750
- Where are you?
- Oh, no, oh, no.

1000
00:44:36,833 --> 00:44:38,041
Is this not the right version?

1001
00:44:38,125 --> 00:44:40,250
What? Where's Jessie? Where's Bullseye?

1002
00:44:40,333 --> 00:44:42,416
I'm a little busy
helping Bonnie right now.

1003
00:44:42,500 --> 00:44:44,291
What on earth happened at that sleepover?

1004
00:44:44,375 --> 00:44:45,458
Excuse me. What are you?

1005
00:44:45,541 --> 00:44:47,000
Are you like some sort of old man toy?

1006
00:44:47,083 --> 00:44:48,083
What?

1007
00:44:48,166 --> 00:44:50,083
She thinks you're old
because you're bald, Woody.

1008
00:44:50,166 --> 00:44:51,875
- Why, you little--
- Where's Jessie?

1009
00:44:51,958 --> 00:44:54,041
What happened to Bonnie?
She looks miserable.

1010
00:44:54,125 --> 00:44:55,750
Uh, the girls may have played
hide-and-seek

1011
00:44:55,833 --> 00:44:57,708
and, um, forgotten to find Bonnie.

1012
00:44:57,791 --> 00:44:59,083
- (all gasp)
- Poor Bonnie.

1013
00:44:59,166 --> 00:45:00,166
How could you let that happen?

1014
00:45:00,250 --> 00:45:02,583
I didn't. You toys did this!

1015
00:45:02,666 --> 00:45:05,333
These girls have been
on The Pond for over a year,

1016
00:45:05,416 --> 00:45:06,416
but Bonnie is behind

1017
00:45:06,500 --> 00:45:09,125
because all of the time
she's been playing with you!

1018
00:45:09,208 --> 00:45:10,750
I need to bring her up to speed fast,

1019
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:11,833
starting with Turtle Tag.

1020
00:45:11,916 --> 00:45:13,750
It's the quickest way for her
to connect with the girls.

1021
00:45:13,833 --> 00:45:15,833
I'm only gonna ask one more time, frog.

1022
00:45:15,916 --> 00:45:17,083
Where is Jessie?

1023
00:45:17,166 --> 00:45:18,500
Not my problem. I'm very busy.

1024
00:45:18,583 --> 00:45:19,875
- (all gasp)
- That's it.

1025
00:45:19,958 --> 00:45:21,291
- We'll make her talk.
- I'll do it, Woody.

1026
00:45:21,375 --> 00:45:22,375
- (grunts)
- Hey! Hey!

1027
00:45:22,458 --> 00:45:23,750
- I got it. I'll--
- I got it, Buzz. No.

1028
00:45:23,833 --> 00:45:25,541
- (Lilypad) Back off, buddy.
- I got this. Ow!

1029
00:45:25,625 --> 00:45:27,125
Do not touch me. Don't touch--

1030
00:45:27,208 --> 00:45:28,500
Where's Jessie?

1031
00:45:29,333 --> 00:45:31,833
Okay. You toys are out of here.

1032
00:45:31,916 --> 00:45:33,333
(♪ ominous music playing)

1033
00:45:33,416 --> 00:45:34,625
(gasps) Wait. She's doing something.

1034
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:38,208
- So long, toys.
- (alarm blaring)

1035
00:45:38,291 --> 00:45:39,125
(shouts)

1036
00:45:39,208 --> 00:45:41,166
- Turn her off!
- Turn her off!

1037
00:45:41,250 --> 00:45:42,666
I can't! I can't! It's not responding!

1038
00:45:42,750 --> 00:45:43,750
I have plastic fingers!

1039
00:45:43,833 --> 00:45:44,833
She's coming.

1040
00:45:45,458 --> 00:45:46,750
(alarm stops)

1041
00:45:51,500 --> 00:45:52,958
You sure you want me to take these toys?

1042
00:45:53,041 --> 00:45:54,166
Mm-hmm.

1043
00:45:54,250 --> 00:45:56,083
Okay. It's your room.

1044
00:45:57,500 --> 00:45:58,500
(gasps)

1045
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:00,000
No!

1046
00:46:00,833 --> 00:46:02,125
They'll be in the garage if you want them.

1047
00:46:02,208 --> 00:46:03,208
Yep.

1048
00:46:06,333 --> 00:46:09,583
(Mr. Pricklepants) I now
pronounce us in storage.

1049
00:46:11,750 --> 00:46:14,125
(chuckles) <i>Playing with you is fun.</i>

1050
00:46:16,833 --> 00:46:18,625
Okay. Now what do we d--

1051
00:46:19,250 --> 00:46:21,583
(♪ melancholy music playing)

1052
00:46:22,375 --> 00:46:23,583
(sighs)

1053
00:46:26,416 --> 00:46:29,125
Don't worry, Buzz. We're gonna find her.

1054
00:46:29,875 --> 00:46:30,875
I promise.

1055
00:46:31,833 --> 00:46:34,416
(sighs)

1056
00:46:35,250 --> 00:46:38,625
Woody, I know it's just
a pretend ceremony,

1057
00:46:38,708 --> 00:46:41,000
and Bonnie usually
decides these things, but…

1058
00:46:42,208 --> 00:46:44,875
Well, if it were up to me,

1059
00:46:46,125 --> 00:46:47,291
you'd be my best man.

1060
00:46:47,375 --> 00:46:48,916
(gasps)

1061
00:46:49,000 --> 00:46:50,291
Buzz, I…

1062
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:52,250
I'd be honored.

1063
00:46:52,333 --> 00:46:54,916
(sighs) But Jessie
will never speak to me again

1064
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:57,166
now that I've let Lily
take charge of the room.

1065
00:46:57,666 --> 00:46:58,916
Wait a min-- Take charge.

1066
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:01,166
- I tried to.
- No, no, no. Buzz, that's it.

1067
00:47:01,250 --> 00:47:02,250
What is?

1068
00:47:02,333 --> 00:47:04,250
(♪ suspenseful music playing)

1069
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:13,000
Tomorrow morning,

1070
00:47:13,083 --> 00:47:15,416
everyone will wake up fully recharged…

1071
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:19,041
except Lilypad.

1072
00:47:19,125 --> 00:47:22,500
And then we'll make Lily
tell us… Where's Jessie?

1073
00:47:27,333 --> 00:47:28,875
(Blaze snoring)

1074
00:47:28,958 --> 00:47:30,708
Oh, finally.

1075
00:47:35,875 --> 00:47:36,958
Psst. Hey.

1076
00:47:37,041 --> 00:47:38,416
(Smarty Pants) It's okay. Just ignore her.

1077
00:47:38,500 --> 00:47:40,000
- (Atlas) Shh, shh.
- (Snappy) Quiet!

1078
00:47:40,083 --> 00:47:41,500
(Smarty Pants) Nobody's home.

1079
00:47:42,125 --> 00:47:44,500
- I can hear you.
- (Snappy) Smarty!

1080
00:47:44,583 --> 00:47:46,541
- What? I used a faraway voice.
- (Atlas) Come on, man!

1081
00:47:46,625 --> 00:47:48,458
- Look. Camera--
- It's Snappy.

1082
00:47:48,541 --> 00:47:49,583
Right, Snappy.

1083
00:47:49,666 --> 00:47:51,375
You said there was a way you could help us

1084
00:47:51,458 --> 00:47:52,958
get to Bonnie, right? So, what is it?

1085
00:47:53,041 --> 00:47:55,083
(Smarty Pants)
She did say that, didn't she?

1086
00:47:55,166 --> 00:47:56,916
That sounds, I don't know…

1087
00:47:57,000 --> 00:47:59,125
- (Snappy) Useful?
- That's it, yeah.

1088
00:47:59,208 --> 00:48:01,458
Too bad we're useless!

1089
00:48:01,541 --> 00:48:03,666
- (Snappy) Right!
- (Atlas) Yeah! Remember?

1090
00:48:04,500 --> 00:48:06,125
- (blusters)
- (sighs)

1091
00:48:06,208 --> 00:48:09,000
I'm sorry I called you useless.

1092
00:48:09,083 --> 00:48:13,833
You three are definitely of use…

1093
00:48:14,375 --> 00:48:15,708
somehow.

1094
00:48:16,500 --> 00:48:18,375
- (Snappy) Worst apology ever.
- (Atlas) Just awful.

1095
00:48:18,458 --> 00:48:20,541
(Smarty Pants) Now I want
an apology for that apology.

1096
00:48:20,625 --> 00:48:22,166
(sighs)

1097
00:48:22,250 --> 00:48:25,583
Please. I know I messed up.

1098
00:48:26,083 --> 00:48:29,166
I was wrong about your kid, Blaze.

1099
00:48:29,250 --> 00:48:33,500
She's creative and silly

1100
00:48:33,583 --> 00:48:36,250
in a way other kids don't really get.

1101
00:48:36,875 --> 00:48:38,208
(stammers) Am I right?

1102
00:48:47,250 --> 00:48:48,625
Go on.

1103
00:48:49,208 --> 00:48:51,583
Well, our kid's like that too.

1104
00:48:51,666 --> 00:48:54,041
And I think they'd really like each other.

1105
00:48:54,125 --> 00:48:56,333
So, fine, if you don't want to help me,

1106
00:48:56,416 --> 00:48:58,291
let's just help our kids.

1107
00:48:59,708 --> 00:49:01,250
All right, twist my handle.

1108
00:49:01,333 --> 00:49:02,750
Yeah! We're making friends.

1109
00:49:02,833 --> 00:49:04,125
- F-R-E-N-D.
- With an "I."

1110
00:49:04,208 --> 00:49:05,208
(Snappy) F-R-I-N-D.

1111
00:49:05,291 --> 00:49:07,250
Great! So, how do we connect them?

1112
00:49:07,333 --> 00:49:10,375
You said your kid's device was
on The Pond like me, right?

1113
00:49:10,458 --> 00:49:14,416
Right! So Smarty, Atlas and I
are all compatible, see?

1114
00:49:14,500 --> 00:49:16,208
And I could take a picture of you.

1115
00:49:16,291 --> 00:49:18,375
- Okay, act like a toy.
- O-Okay.

1116
00:49:20,333 --> 00:49:22,291
Uh, not very photogenic, are they?

1117
00:49:22,375 --> 00:49:24,083
- And Atlas can add text to it.
- Mm-hmm.

1118
00:49:25,583 --> 00:49:27,625
- Then we post it on The Pond.
- (Atlas) Yep.

1119
00:49:27,708 --> 00:49:28,708
Where Bonnie is!

1120
00:49:28,791 --> 00:49:30,125
(all) Ta-da!

1121
00:49:30,208 --> 00:49:31,958
- Great! So, you sent it?
- (♪ gentle music playing)

1122
00:49:32,041 --> 00:49:33,416
No. Still going.

1123
00:49:33,500 --> 00:49:35,000
(sighs)

1124
00:49:37,083 --> 00:49:38,208
How about now?

1125
00:49:38,291 --> 00:49:40,708
(exclaims) Still going.

1126
00:49:40,791 --> 00:49:42,750
Still going? How is that possible?

1127
00:49:42,833 --> 00:49:44,916
Look at my eyes! The little
toilet roll's still spinning.

1128
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:46,583
I'm only as fast as my operating system.

1129
00:49:46,666 --> 00:49:48,666
So just slow your roll, all right?

1130
00:49:49,916 --> 00:49:51,500
- (chimes)
- There. It's sent.

1131
00:49:51,583 --> 00:49:54,083
Finally. Now what?

1132
00:49:54,166 --> 00:49:55,208
Now, we wait.

1133
00:49:55,291 --> 00:49:56,500
Yeah, everyone's still asleep.

1134
00:49:56,583 --> 00:49:58,583
We gotta wait for Bonnie
to wake up and see the post.

1135
00:49:58,666 --> 00:50:01,083
(groans, sighs)

1136
00:50:03,208 --> 00:50:05,875
Hey, I know! We could play a game.

1137
00:50:05,958 --> 00:50:06,791
- Yes!
- Yeah!

1138
00:50:06,875 --> 00:50:07,708
- A game?
- Yeah!

1139
00:50:07,791 --> 00:50:09,083
It was Blaze's favorite.

1140
00:50:09,166 --> 00:50:10,750
It's called "Pick the Poop."

1141
00:50:10,833 --> 00:50:11,958
You try and hit the button

1142
00:50:12,041 --> 00:50:13,916
when the poop shows up over it.

1143
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:15,208
Hey, Smarty.

1144
00:50:16,083 --> 00:50:19,916
I will never play that game.

1145
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:23,166
(chuckles) They all say that.

1146
00:50:24,375 --> 00:50:26,375
(insects chirping)

1147
00:50:26,458 --> 00:50:27,750
(child laughing)

1148
00:50:27,833 --> 00:50:28,666
(sibling) Come on!

1149
00:50:28,750 --> 00:50:30,625
- It's my turn.
- (mom) Okay, you two.

1150
00:50:30,708 --> 00:50:32,875
Time to stop playing with your new toy.

1151
00:50:32,958 --> 00:50:34,791
- It's bedtime.
- (children groan)

1152
00:50:34,875 --> 00:50:36,875
- Already?
- Do we have to?

1153
00:50:36,958 --> 00:50:38,791
- (mom) Yeah, come on.
- (children groan)

1154
00:50:38,875 --> 00:50:40,875
(♪ tense music playing)

1155
00:51:12,458 --> 00:51:13,666
(laptop beeps)

1156
00:51:13,750 --> 00:51:14,750
Huh?

1157
00:51:24,125 --> 00:51:29,291
(mom) "And they had splendid
games together, in whispers,

1158
00:51:29,375 --> 00:51:32,125
when Nana had gone away to her supper

1159
00:51:32,208 --> 00:51:34,000
and left the night-light burning

1160
00:51:34,083 --> 00:51:35,666
on the mantelpiece.

1161
00:51:36,250 --> 00:51:39,375
And when the boy dropped off to sleep,

1162
00:51:39,458 --> 00:51:43,708
the rabbit would snuggle down close under

1163
00:51:43,791 --> 00:51:45,333
- his little, warm chin…"
- (beeping)

1164
00:51:45,416 --> 00:51:46,416
Sir.

1165
00:51:46,500 --> 00:51:49,875
"…and dream with the boy's hands

1166
00:51:49,958 --> 00:51:53,541
clasped close round him all night."

1167
00:51:59,958 --> 00:52:01,208
Hmm.

1168
00:52:02,416 --> 00:52:04,625
- (gasp) Star Command.
- Star Command.

1169
00:52:04,708 --> 00:52:06,083
- Star Command.
- Star Command.

1170
00:52:12,583 --> 00:52:14,750
(all) Star Command.

1171
00:52:16,500 --> 00:52:18,833
- (birds chirping)
- (groans)

1172
00:52:19,958 --> 00:52:23,000
(yawns, sighs)

1173
00:52:24,166 --> 00:52:25,416
What? No, no, no!

1174
00:52:25,500 --> 00:52:27,000
Dad! Dad!

1175
00:52:27,083 --> 00:52:28,125
What? What is it?

1176
00:52:28,208 --> 00:52:30,625
Lily's not working!
I'm missing Turtle Tag!

1177
00:52:30,708 --> 00:52:32,958
Kara, Chelsea and Heidi
play it every morning.

1178
00:52:33,041 --> 00:52:35,166
- I can't miss it, Dad!
- It's okay.

1179
00:52:35,250 --> 00:52:36,250
I plugged it back in.

1180
00:52:36,333 --> 00:52:37,625
We just need to wait for it to charge.

1181
00:52:37,708 --> 00:52:39,875
But it's not okay!
I'm gonna miss the game!

1182
00:52:39,958 --> 00:52:41,958
Sweetie, there's nothing
we can do for now.

1183
00:52:42,041 --> 00:52:43,875
- (Bonnie groans)
- (door closes)

1184
00:52:43,958 --> 00:52:46,500
Aha! Success, huh? Look at that.

1185
00:52:46,583 --> 00:52:47,583
That's phase one.

1186
00:52:47,666 --> 00:52:49,375
- And now, phase two.
- Phase two.

1187
00:52:49,875 --> 00:52:51,541
Well, I thought I was gonna
initiate phase two.

1188
00:52:51,625 --> 00:52:53,916
I initiate phase two.
We thumb wrestled over this.

1189
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:55,041
All right, fine.

1190
00:52:55,583 --> 00:52:57,708
And then we'll have a little talk

1191
00:52:57,791 --> 00:52:59,666
with our froggy friend.

1192
00:53:00,375 --> 00:53:03,291
- (toy beeping)
- (Blaze snoring)

1193
00:53:03,375 --> 00:53:05,166
(grunting)

1194
00:53:05,250 --> 00:53:07,958
- One, two, one, two, two…
- I hate this game.

1195
00:53:08,041 --> 00:53:09,708
- …one, two, one…
- Please make it stop.

1196
00:53:11,208 --> 00:53:12,958
- Mighty Wiper!
- (Atlas shushes)

1197
00:53:13,041 --> 00:53:15,041
- Again, again, again!
- I think you need a break.

1198
00:53:15,125 --> 00:53:16,125
I can't feel my buttons.

1199
00:53:16,208 --> 00:53:19,416
- Just one more time! Come on!
- That's enough play for now.

1200
00:53:19,500 --> 00:53:20,500
Play? (scoffs)

1201
00:53:20,583 --> 00:53:22,541
That's just a game. That's not playing.

1202
00:53:22,625 --> 00:53:23,541
What's the difference?

1203
00:53:23,625 --> 00:53:25,083
You know, real play.

1204
00:53:26,791 --> 00:53:28,291
You're kidding, right?

1205
00:53:28,375 --> 00:53:30,208
You've never seen Blaze play with a toy?

1206
00:53:31,583 --> 00:53:32,875
How long were you guys with her?

1207
00:53:32,958 --> 00:53:33,958
- Three months.
- Ten months.

1208
00:53:34,041 --> 00:53:35,041
- Six months.
- Months?

1209
00:53:35,125 --> 00:53:36,000
What? Too long?

1210
00:53:36,083 --> 00:53:39,166
Too short! (groans)
Guys, you missed all the fun!

1211
00:53:39,250 --> 00:53:40,125
Hey, we're fun.

1212
00:53:40,208 --> 00:53:42,958
I mean fun, fun. Make-believe fun.

1213
00:53:47,375 --> 00:53:48,708
Just look at her.

1214
00:53:51,375 --> 00:53:53,375
Oh, yeah. She plays.

1215
00:53:53,458 --> 00:53:55,166
Oh, yeah? Prove it.

1216
00:53:55,666 --> 00:53:59,083
Okay, Smarty Pants. We will.

1217
00:54:01,083 --> 00:54:03,916
(sniffs, snorting)

1218
00:54:04,000 --> 00:54:05,416
(groans)

1219
00:54:06,041 --> 00:54:07,375
Morning, Jimmy.

1220
00:54:08,541 --> 00:54:11,125
Ready for breakfast? Hmm?

1221
00:54:15,750 --> 00:54:16,583
Whoa.

1222
00:54:17,125 --> 00:54:19,916
Hey, Mom! Where'd you find the cowgirl?

1223
00:54:20,000 --> 00:54:21,000
(chuckles)

1224
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:23,208
<i>I ain't afraid of nothin', partner.</i>

1225
00:54:23,291 --> 00:54:26,375
- (chuckles)
<i>- Yeehaw! Let's play!</i>

1226
00:54:26,458 --> 00:54:27,458
(gasps)

1227
00:54:28,375 --> 00:54:29,625
Yeah.

1228
00:54:31,500 --> 00:54:32,791
(chuckles)

1229
00:54:32,875 --> 00:54:34,500
Wait a minute.

1230
00:54:36,958 --> 00:54:38,208
(Blaze chuckles) Hmm.

1231
00:54:38,291 --> 00:54:39,291
Neigh!

1232
00:54:39,375 --> 00:54:41,000
Well, flush me.

1233
00:54:41,083 --> 00:54:43,041
Blaze is actually gonna play.

1234
00:54:43,125 --> 00:54:45,791
(vocalizing) Here we go!

1235
00:54:45,875 --> 00:54:47,708
(♪ ballroom music playing)

1236
00:54:48,541 --> 00:54:49,791
- M'la-- (gasps)
- (gasps, chuckles)

1237
00:54:51,458 --> 00:54:53,708
M'lady Davenport,

1238
00:54:54,750 --> 00:54:57,333
I present Her Royal Highness,

1239
00:54:57,416 --> 00:54:59,500
Jimmy Queen.

1240
00:54:59,583 --> 00:55:01,000
(snorting)

1241
00:55:01,083 --> 00:55:04,291
(clears throat)
Your Highness, how kind of you

1242
00:55:04,375 --> 00:55:05,958
to invite me to your royal ball--

1243
00:55:06,041 --> 00:55:08,458
(babbling)

1244
00:55:08,541 --> 00:55:10,750
Jimmy! This is your big moment.

1245
00:55:10,833 --> 00:55:13,166
- (snorting)
- (toys beeping)

1246
00:55:14,458 --> 00:55:16,250
What you got there, Jimmy?

1247
00:55:16,333 --> 00:55:17,666
(snorting)

1248
00:55:17,750 --> 00:55:19,875
Whoa.

1249
00:55:20,708 --> 00:55:22,916
(chuckling) I can't believe
I still have these.

1250
00:55:23,708 --> 00:55:25,625
(gasps) Wait a minute.

1251
00:55:27,041 --> 00:55:30,041
(♪ suspenseful music playing)

1252
00:55:30,125 --> 00:55:31,333
(Snappy) <i>Agent Clydesdale,</i>

1253
00:55:31,416 --> 00:55:33,083
<i>your suitor is approaching now.</i>

1254
00:55:33,166 --> 00:55:34,166
(gasps)

1255
00:55:34,250 --> 00:55:37,333
So, we meet again, Agent Sheet-land.

1256
00:55:37,416 --> 00:55:39,000
It's pronounced Shet-land. "Shet."

1257
00:55:39,083 --> 00:55:40,250
That's what I said.

1258
00:55:40,333 --> 00:55:42,166
Well, Agent Clydesdale, or should I say,

1259
00:55:42,250 --> 00:55:44,500
Lady Davenport, have you spotted it yet?

1260
00:55:44,583 --> 00:55:45,791
You mean, the bomb?

1261
00:55:45,875 --> 00:55:47,208
Yes! Shh! Quiet!

1262
00:55:47,291 --> 00:55:48,750
Snappy, do you have eyes on it?

1263
00:55:48,833 --> 00:55:50,625
Not yet. Atlas, do you copy?

1264
00:55:52,125 --> 00:55:54,291
Agents! The bomb is right on top of you!

1265
00:55:54,375 --> 00:55:56,708
- (beeping)
- (gasps) Where? Where?

1266
00:55:56,791 --> 00:55:57,833
(laughs)

1267
00:55:57,916 --> 00:56:01,458
Where you never suspected,
Agent Clydesdale!

1268
00:56:01,541 --> 00:56:04,166
- (laughing)
- (guests gasping)

1269
00:56:04,875 --> 00:56:07,208
- (gasps)
- (laughs)

1270
00:56:07,291 --> 00:56:09,458
But where is the bomb?

1271
00:56:09,541 --> 00:56:11,708
(beeping)

1272
00:56:15,541 --> 00:56:16,583
(exclaims)

1273
00:56:18,208 --> 00:56:19,583
She's coming to, Buzz.

1274
00:56:19,666 --> 00:56:20,708
(tablet beeping)

1275
00:56:20,791 --> 00:56:21,791
Hurry it up.

1276
00:56:21,875 --> 00:56:23,291
(Buzz) I'm trying, Woody!

1277
00:56:23,375 --> 00:56:25,916
What… What happened?

1278
00:56:26,000 --> 00:56:28,375
Wait. What did you do to my battery?

1279
00:56:28,458 --> 00:56:29,791
What we'll do again if you don't tell us

1280
00:56:29,875 --> 00:56:31,416
what happened to Jessie and Bullseye.

1281
00:56:31,500 --> 00:56:33,291
What time is it? (gasps)

1282
00:56:33,375 --> 00:56:35,208
Oh, no! This is not good.

1283
00:56:35,291 --> 00:56:37,708
The girls got a head start
on Turtle Tag without Bonnie!

1284
00:56:37,791 --> 00:56:40,000
There's been one, two,
three inside jokes already.

1285
00:56:40,083 --> 00:56:41,083
This is a disaster!

1286
00:56:41,166 --> 00:56:43,541
Enough with the silly games.
Where's Jessie and Bullseye?

1287
00:56:43,625 --> 00:56:46,416
Silly? This is serious, Stuffalo Bill!

1288
00:56:46,500 --> 00:56:47,833
Bonnie is missing out.

1289
00:56:47,916 --> 00:56:48,916
Stuffalo Bill?

1290
00:56:49,000 --> 00:56:50,916
Want her to make friends? This is how!

1291
00:56:51,000 --> 00:56:53,041
Now keep your little
plastic hands away from me

1292
00:56:53,125 --> 00:56:55,041
or I will set off my alarm.

1293
00:56:55,125 --> 00:56:56,500
I thought you'd say as much.

1294
00:56:56,583 --> 00:56:58,833
Buzz, bring in "Sammy Two."

1295
00:56:58,916 --> 00:57:02,000
- No. No. Absolutely not.
- (grunting)

1296
00:57:02,750 --> 00:57:03,958
- Oh, no, no, no--
- (alarm blaring)

1297
00:57:04,041 --> 00:57:05,291
- (Buzz) Yes. (chuckles)
- (alarm stops)

1298
00:57:05,375 --> 00:57:07,333
- Okay, try "settings."
- You mean this?

1299
00:57:07,416 --> 00:57:09,666
- That's a gear symbol.
- Okay, got it. Now what?

1300
00:57:09,750 --> 00:57:10,750
Reduce her screen time to zero.

1301
00:57:11,750 --> 00:57:12,791
(Buzz) The shortest is an hour.

1302
00:57:14,458 --> 00:57:16,041
- What?
- "Horse grill"? Who is that?

1303
00:57:16,125 --> 00:57:17,333
"Horse girl."

1304
00:57:17,416 --> 00:57:20,000
- She's talking about Jessie.
- Well, then open it. (gasps)

1305
00:57:20,083 --> 00:57:21,375
- Whoa!
- (grunting)

1306
00:57:21,458 --> 00:57:22,625
(tablet chimes)

1307
00:57:22,708 --> 00:57:25,041
- (Lilypad exclaims)
- (Woody) My hips.

1308
00:57:25,125 --> 00:57:26,750
Enjoy the garage, suckers!

1309
00:57:26,833 --> 00:57:28,125
- No, no, no! Lily!
- Wait. Hey!

1310
00:57:28,208 --> 00:57:29,041
(gasps)

1311
00:57:29,125 --> 00:57:30,375
<i>Yes, can I help you?</i>

1312
00:57:31,125 --> 00:57:32,333
Huh?

1313
00:57:32,416 --> 00:57:34,500
- Wait a minute. (shushes)
- Fascinating.

1314
00:57:34,583 --> 00:57:37,208
Lily, bring back that "horse girl" post.

1315
00:57:37,291 --> 00:57:38,458
(distorted buzzing)

1316
00:57:38,541 --> 00:57:39,583
<i>Okay.</i>

1317
00:57:39,666 --> 00:57:42,750
Oh, she has to do what you say.

1318
00:57:42,833 --> 00:57:45,000
- (screams)
- (gasps, grunts)

1319
00:57:45,083 --> 00:57:46,375
- She's getting away, Buzz!
- Lily!

1320
00:57:46,458 --> 00:57:47,833
- Hey, Lily!
- Hey, stop her!

1321
00:57:47,916 --> 00:57:48,916
- Hey, Lily!
<i>- Yes?</i>

1322
00:57:49,000 --> 00:57:50,875
- Open that post!
<i>- Okay!</i>

1323
00:57:50,958 --> 00:57:52,958
- (gasps) Jessie.
- Bonnie's gotta see this.

1324
00:57:53,041 --> 00:57:55,000
(Buzz) Show her again.
Where is she? Hey, Lily.

1325
00:57:55,083 --> 00:57:55,916
- Hey, Lily!
<i>- Yes?</i>

1326
00:57:56,000 --> 00:57:57,041
- Show the post.
<i>- Can I help you?</i>

1327
00:57:57,125 --> 00:57:58,000
- Share it everywhere!
- Share!

1328
00:57:58,083 --> 00:57:58,916
<i>- Yes!</i>
- Share!

1329
00:57:59,916 --> 00:58:00,916
We did it!

1330
00:58:01,000 --> 00:58:02,000
So, where did it go?

1331
00:58:02,083 --> 00:58:03,125
Lily…

1332
00:58:03,208 --> 00:58:05,041
(all grunting)

1333
00:58:06,250 --> 00:58:07,250
(Lilypad panting)

1334
00:58:07,333 --> 00:58:08,625
- (machine whirring)
- (gasps)

1335
00:58:09,791 --> 00:58:11,791
- (Buzz) The printer! Yes!
- (Woody laughs)

1336
00:58:11,875 --> 00:58:12,708
(Bonnie) Okay, I'm done.

1337
00:58:12,791 --> 00:58:14,083
(Mom) Bonnie, you haven't
finished your breakfast.

1338
00:58:14,166 --> 00:58:15,916
- (Bonnie) No, I'm done.
- (gasps)

1339
00:58:17,458 --> 00:58:20,291
I'm missing Turtle Tag, Mom.
They're playing without me.

1340
00:58:20,375 --> 00:58:22,875
- (groans, pants)
- (Lilypad laughs)

1341
00:58:22,958 --> 00:58:24,125
Now what, Deputy?

1342
00:58:24,208 --> 00:58:26,041
Well, you're the deputy, Deputy.

1343
00:58:28,541 --> 00:58:30,208
What's this all about, Bonnie?

1344
00:58:32,125 --> 00:58:34,041
- Huh?
- (groans)

1345
00:58:37,166 --> 00:58:39,166
So, why did you put her toys
in the garage?

1346
00:58:39,250 --> 00:58:41,208
Uh, because Bonnie asked me to.

1347
00:58:41,291 --> 00:58:43,291
- Remember, sweetie?
- No.

1348
00:58:43,375 --> 00:58:45,208
(Dad) Well, I don't think
Lilypad texted me.

1349
00:58:45,291 --> 00:58:48,666
They're gone. She really does
have Jessie and Bullseye.

1350
00:58:48,750 --> 00:58:50,375
I hope they're okay.

1351
00:58:50,458 --> 00:58:52,083
Okay, we've gotten the queen to safety.

1352
00:58:52,166 --> 00:58:54,791
Yes. You can do this, Agent Clydesdale.

1353
00:58:54,875 --> 00:58:56,458
One of these buttons defuses the bomb.

1354
00:58:56,541 --> 00:58:58,458
But which one, Agent "Sheetland"?

1355
00:58:58,541 --> 00:59:00,625
"Shet"! (sobbing) It's "Shet"!

1356
00:59:00,708 --> 00:59:02,583
(beeping)

1357
00:59:03,166 --> 00:59:04,166
(beeping stops)

1358
00:59:05,833 --> 00:59:07,791
Boom! (imitates explosion)

1359
00:59:07,875 --> 00:59:10,958
Oh, no! (imitates explosion) (screams)

1360
00:59:11,041 --> 00:59:13,625
(Blaze's mom) Blaze! Hon!
It's time to feed Daffodil.

1361
00:59:13,708 --> 00:59:15,708
(kisses) Okay! (chuckles)

1362
00:59:15,791 --> 00:59:17,666
Come on, Your Majesty.

1363
00:59:18,666 --> 00:59:19,958
(Blaze's mom) Thanks, babe!

1364
00:59:20,041 --> 00:59:21,041
(door closes)

1365
00:59:21,125 --> 00:59:21,958
(Snappy laughs)

1366
00:59:22,041 --> 00:59:24,416
- Holy cow! Wow!
- That was so cool! (squeals)

1367
00:59:24,500 --> 00:59:26,791
- I was a spy! What?
- Yeah, you were!

1368
00:59:26,875 --> 00:59:28,083
- You were the best spy!
- Wow.

1369
00:59:28,166 --> 00:59:29,708
(both chuckling)

1370
00:59:29,791 --> 00:59:31,875
- Smarty?
- (sobbing)

1371
00:59:31,958 --> 00:59:34,083
That was so beautiful.

1372
00:59:34,625 --> 00:59:37,375
That, my friend, was playin'.

1373
00:59:37,458 --> 00:59:39,916
- Oh, boy, did we.
- I feel so alive!

1374
00:59:40,000 --> 00:59:41,916
Is that what being a toy is like, Sheriff?

1375
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:43,958
Well, yeah, it's… Wait, hold up.

1376
00:59:44,041 --> 00:59:46,750
You never called me
sheriff before in a nice way.

1377
00:59:46,833 --> 00:59:47,958
But, well, now I get it.

1378
00:59:48,041 --> 00:59:50,416
Blaze really is perfect for Bonnie.

1379
00:59:50,500 --> 00:59:52,666
Playing with her feels just the same.

1380
00:59:52,750 --> 00:59:55,166
- Your kid plays like that too?
- (chimes)

1381
00:59:55,250 --> 00:59:56,250
(all gasp)

1382
00:59:57,958 --> 00:59:59,125
- (Jessie gasps)
- (gasps) It's her!

1383
00:59:59,208 --> 01:00:00,875
She saw the post! It's Bonnie!

1384
01:00:00,958 --> 01:00:02,375
- Go on! Do it.
- Text her back.

1385
01:00:02,458 --> 01:00:03,916
- Go on.
- Text her back.

1386
01:00:04,000 --> 01:00:06,708
(all chanting)
Text her back! Text her back.

1387
01:00:06,791 --> 01:00:09,166
Okay, okay, how do I do that?

1388
01:00:09,833 --> 01:00:11,958
(tablet beeping)

1389
01:00:18,625 --> 01:00:20,666
(beeping)

1390
01:00:24,958 --> 01:00:28,041
- (sighs)
- What? Oh, yes!

1391
01:00:28,125 --> 01:00:29,916
- All right!
- She's coming.

1392
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:32,250
- Bonnie's coming here.
- (Snappy) I knew she would.

1393
01:00:32,333 --> 01:00:34,500
Blaze and Bonnie are gonna meet.

1394
01:00:34,583 --> 01:00:36,458
- (beeping)
- Smarty, what are you typing?

1395
01:00:36,541 --> 01:00:38,458
- Delete that right now.
- What?

1396
01:00:38,541 --> 01:00:40,708
I'm just trying to get some
batteries out of the deal.

1397
01:00:42,083 --> 01:00:43,333
So, what's going on?

1398
01:00:43,416 --> 01:00:44,458
Slink, talk to me.

1399
01:00:44,958 --> 01:00:46,791
Hard to hear. A lot of commotion.

1400
01:00:46,875 --> 01:00:48,583
I bet they're arguing over
getting rid of us.

1401
01:00:48,666 --> 01:00:50,541
(exclaims) Are we getting donated?

1402
01:00:50,625 --> 01:00:53,708
- Mmm. Doughnuts.
- No, sweetie. Donated.

1403
01:00:53,791 --> 01:00:55,833
Wow. I love her,
but this is gonna be hard.

1404
01:00:55,916 --> 01:00:58,958
Shh! Quiet! I hear something.
Like tiny footsteps.

1405
01:00:59,041 --> 01:01:00,875
- Aw. Kind of cute.
- (footsteps approaching)

1406
01:01:00,958 --> 01:01:02,166
(shouting)

1407
01:01:02,250 --> 01:01:03,833
- Look out!
- Bonnie's coming!

1408
01:01:06,541 --> 01:01:07,583
Come on, Mom.

1409
01:01:07,666 --> 01:01:09,458
(Woody) Oh, no, Lily's going too.

1410
01:01:09,541 --> 01:01:10,833
(Bonnie's mom) Hold on,
Bonnie. I'm sure your toys

1411
01:01:10,916 --> 01:01:11,958
aren't going to run off on their own.

1412
01:01:12,041 --> 01:01:13,125
All right, Buzz, you've gotta stay here.

1413
01:01:13,208 --> 01:01:14,875
- I'm going with them.
- Why? Why just you?

1414
01:01:14,958 --> 01:01:16,541
Look, I just have more
field experience than you.

1415
01:01:16,625 --> 01:01:17,583
That is all.

1416
01:01:18,375 --> 01:01:19,833
You don't think I can do it.

1417
01:01:19,916 --> 01:01:21,916
No, I just think I can do it a little bit…

1418
01:01:22,000 --> 01:01:24,166
- (car engine starts)
- …better.

1419
01:01:24,250 --> 01:01:26,375
(gasps) You don't deserve this.

1420
01:01:26,458 --> 01:01:28,583
- Buzz, come on. I was only--
- Jessie put me in charge.

1421
01:01:28,666 --> 01:01:30,833
Which is why you should
stay here and watch the room.

1422
01:01:30,916 --> 01:01:32,666
There is no room without Jessie.

1423
01:01:32,750 --> 01:01:34,583
Buzz, no! (groans)

1424
01:01:34,666 --> 01:01:37,166
(♪ dramatic music playing)

1425
01:01:37,250 --> 01:01:39,458
(panting, grunting)

1426
01:01:40,500 --> 01:01:42,958
(breathing heavily)

1427
01:01:43,041 --> 01:01:43,958
(grunts)

1428
01:01:44,041 --> 01:01:46,375
Nice poncho. (scoffs)

1429
01:01:46,458 --> 01:01:48,416
It's good to see them fighting again.

1430
01:01:48,500 --> 01:01:49,666
(Slinky Dog) It sure is.

1431
01:01:56,958 --> 01:01:59,083
How did your toys get
all the way out here?

1432
01:01:59,166 --> 01:02:00,500
(grunts)

1433
01:02:00,583 --> 01:02:01,583
(tablet chirps)

1434
01:02:07,333 --> 01:02:08,958
(gasps)

1435
01:02:15,791 --> 01:02:16,791
(gasps)

1436
01:02:23,916 --> 01:02:27,041
Oh, how 'bout this one?
Ah, look at those puppies.

1437
01:02:27,125 --> 01:02:28,541
I'm saving that one.

1438
01:02:28,625 --> 01:02:30,625
Yeah, they came with the
latest update this morning.

1439
01:02:30,708 --> 01:02:31,916
I know. It never gets old.

1440
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:33,000
(chuckling) She's here.

1441
01:02:33,083 --> 01:02:34,583
Careful, Snappy. Dad might see you.

1442
01:02:34,666 --> 01:02:37,375
No way. He'll be showing off
those new backgrounds forever.

1443
01:02:38,000 --> 01:02:40,458
(gasps) That's her! That's Bonnie!

1444
01:02:40,541 --> 01:02:43,083
- Bullseye, she's really here!
- (blusters)

1445
01:02:44,375 --> 01:02:46,083
Bonnie, come on, let's go.

1446
01:02:50,625 --> 01:02:54,291
(coughs) Buzz, listen. I really just…

1447
01:02:54,375 --> 01:02:55,625
(Woody groans)

1448
01:02:58,125 --> 01:02:59,291
(Atlas) Aw. (chuckles)

1449
01:02:59,375 --> 01:03:01,041
It was nothing. It was nothing.

1450
01:03:01,125 --> 01:03:04,125
Thanks, fellas.
Pretty glad I met you devices.

1451
01:03:04,208 --> 01:03:06,416
Ah, don't be dumping us
something you can't flush.

1452
01:03:06,500 --> 01:03:08,541
- (doorbell rings)
- (gasps) It's her!

1453
01:03:10,875 --> 01:03:12,458
Hello. Can I help you?

1454
01:03:12,541 --> 01:03:14,916
Hi. I'm so sorry to bother you,

1455
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:17,000
but we got this message
from your daughter.

1456
01:03:17,083 --> 01:03:19,458
She seems to have found
my daughter's toys.

1457
01:03:19,541 --> 01:03:21,041
- Are they in there?
- (Blaze's mom) Oh, okay.

1458
01:03:21,125 --> 01:03:22,416
I'll have her get 'em.

1459
01:03:22,500 --> 01:03:24,333
- Blaze! Honey?
- (Blaze) Yeah?

1460
01:03:24,416 --> 01:03:26,791
Can you bring down
those two rag dolls you found?

1461
01:03:26,875 --> 01:03:29,083
- Their owner's here.
- (Blaze) Okay!

1462
01:03:29,166 --> 01:03:31,458
- That's our cue.
- (footsteps approaching)

1463
01:03:41,208 --> 01:03:42,208
(gasps)

1464
01:03:42,291 --> 01:03:44,333
Blaze, this is, uh…

1465
01:03:44,833 --> 01:03:46,250
(Bonnie's mom) This is Bonnie.

1466
01:03:46,333 --> 01:03:47,333
(Blaze's mom) Hello, Bonnie.

1467
01:03:47,416 --> 01:03:49,375
Hi. Are these your toys?

1468
01:03:56,375 --> 01:03:58,375
I don't play with toys anymore.

1469
01:03:58,458 --> 01:04:01,708
It's just they're antiques.

1470
01:04:04,166 --> 01:04:05,791
They do look pretty old.

1471
01:04:06,416 --> 01:04:08,708
Must be worth something at least, right?

1472
01:04:10,833 --> 01:04:12,000
No, they're not.

1473
01:04:13,250 --> 01:04:14,500
You should keep 'em.

1474
01:04:17,166 --> 01:04:18,291
(both gasp)

1475
01:04:18,375 --> 01:04:19,750
- (gasps)
- Oh, no.

1476
01:04:21,250 --> 01:04:23,125
Bonnie, you don't want them?

1477
01:04:28,416 --> 01:04:31,916
(stammers) Are you sure? Bonnie? Bonnie?

1478
01:04:32,708 --> 01:04:33,958
I don't know what's come over her.

1479
01:04:34,041 --> 01:04:35,833
I'm so sorry to have bothered you.

1480
01:04:35,916 --> 01:04:37,083
It's all right.

1481
01:04:37,166 --> 01:04:40,166
If you ever change your mind,
Bonnie, just let me know.

1482
01:04:40,250 --> 01:04:42,416
(♪ mournful music playing)

1483
01:04:48,583 --> 01:04:49,583
(door closes)

1484
01:04:49,666 --> 01:04:51,166
I don't get it. What just happened?

1485
01:04:51,250 --> 01:04:52,708
What is going on, Bonnie?

1486
01:04:53,875 --> 01:04:55,333
Okay, I guess we're going.

1487
01:04:56,166 --> 01:04:58,458
- (sniffles)
- (car door opens, closes)

1488
01:05:01,583 --> 01:05:03,625
(all gasp, grunt)

1489
01:05:03,708 --> 01:05:05,083
(footsteps approaching)

1490
01:05:12,833 --> 01:05:14,250
(door creaks)

1491
01:05:15,541 --> 01:05:16,583
(gasps)

1492
01:05:16,666 --> 01:05:19,791
Come on, Bullseye! Quick!
Before they drive away!

1493
01:05:19,875 --> 01:05:21,208
(grunting)

1494
01:05:21,791 --> 01:05:23,250
It's… It's too late for me,

1495
01:05:23,333 --> 01:05:25,250
Bullseye, but maybe not for you.

1496
01:05:25,333 --> 01:05:26,916
- Please, not for you.
- (blusters)

1497
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:30,458
(grunts, breathing heavily)

1498
01:05:31,250 --> 01:05:32,500
- (whinnies)
- (Jessie sighs)

1499
01:05:34,708 --> 01:05:37,208
- Sheriff?
- Jessie? A-Are you okay?

1500
01:05:37,291 --> 01:05:38,708
W-What just happened?

1501
01:05:38,791 --> 01:05:40,291
She ditched you, Jessie.

1502
01:05:40,375 --> 01:05:41,958
Because of you!

1503
01:05:42,041 --> 01:05:44,291
Because of all you darn devices

1504
01:05:44,375 --> 01:05:46,166
making kids act older.

1505
01:05:46,250 --> 01:05:48,208
You stole all our time.

1506
01:05:48,291 --> 01:05:51,083
I wanted to make a difference.
I needed to make a difference.

1507
01:05:51,166 --> 01:05:52,500
And you ruined it.

1508
01:05:52,583 --> 01:05:53,583
- Ow.
- (gasps)

1509
01:05:53,666 --> 01:05:55,708
- Smarty, you okay?
- I'm-I'm sorry.

1510
01:05:55,791 --> 01:05:59,041
- Are you hurt? Did you crack?
- I'm fine. I'm fine. (sighs)

1511
01:05:59,125 --> 01:06:01,208
For a rag doll, you throw
quite a punch, cowgir…

1512
01:06:02,083 --> 01:06:03,458
Cowgirl?

1513
01:06:04,833 --> 01:06:06,458
- (devices gasp)
- (Bullseye whinnies)

1514
01:06:06,541 --> 01:06:07,583
(Snappy) Jessie?

1515
01:06:14,208 --> 01:06:15,750
(whistles)

1516
01:06:17,416 --> 01:06:19,083
Uh, Sheriff?

1517
01:06:19,166 --> 01:06:20,833
I'm sorry, Smarty.

1518
01:06:20,916 --> 01:06:22,125
It's not you.

1519
01:06:23,041 --> 01:06:25,208
I'm the one that's useless.

1520
01:06:25,291 --> 01:06:26,625
- (devices gasp)
- (blusters)

1521
01:06:29,583 --> 01:06:30,583
(whinnies)

1522
01:06:37,666 --> 01:06:38,958
(gasps) Bullseye!

1523
01:06:41,500 --> 01:06:44,083
Poor Jessie. Gotta find a way in.

1524
01:06:45,458 --> 01:06:48,083
Buzz. Buzz, where are you going?

1525
01:06:48,166 --> 01:06:50,166
Let's talk about this. (groans)

1526
01:06:50,250 --> 01:06:51,958
- (electronic wailing)
- Huh?

1527
01:06:53,791 --> 01:06:56,333
Uh, what… what is going on?

1528
01:06:56,416 --> 01:06:57,625
- State your name.
- (Woody) Whoa, whoa.

1529
01:06:57,708 --> 01:06:59,708
- And your purpose.
- Hey, guys. (stammers)

1530
01:06:59,791 --> 01:07:01,541
- Take him in.
- Guys! Whoa!

1531
01:07:02,166 --> 01:07:03,166
(groaning)

1532
01:07:03,250 --> 01:07:05,000
- Wait, wait. What's going on?
- (Jimmy Dean snorting)

1533
01:07:05,083 --> 01:07:06,750
(screams) My poncho!

1534
01:07:07,250 --> 01:07:08,250
Quiet, assassin!

1535
01:07:08,333 --> 01:07:11,000
(grunts) Assassin? No, I can't…

1536
01:07:11,083 --> 01:07:12,166
(straining)

1537
01:07:12,250 --> 01:07:13,750
- Buzz?
- (all gasp)

1538
01:07:13,833 --> 01:07:15,875
How do you know who we are? Who sent you?

1539
01:07:15,958 --> 01:07:18,125
(Woody) Oh, geez! What… I…

1540
01:07:18,208 --> 01:07:20,250
- Talk!
- (screams)

1541
01:07:20,333 --> 01:07:22,083
- (snorting)
- Talk about what?

1542
01:07:22,166 --> 01:07:24,166
- What am I supposed to know?
- You bear a holster.

1543
01:07:24,250 --> 01:07:27,166
You were positioned outside
our leader's stronghold.

1544
01:07:27,250 --> 01:07:29,000
You are an agent of Zurg!

1545
01:07:29,083 --> 01:07:30,583
Zurg? No! Hey!

1546
01:07:30,666 --> 01:07:32,166
I don't even know who your leader is!

1547
01:07:32,250 --> 01:07:34,708
Liar! You wish to harm
the red-haired maiden

1548
01:07:34,791 --> 01:07:36,208
who bears the mark of Star Command.

1549
01:07:36,291 --> 01:07:37,500
- Jessie.
- (Woody) No.

1550
01:07:37,583 --> 01:07:39,250
- Wait!
- (Woody grunting)

1551
01:07:39,333 --> 01:07:41,375
He is not an agent of Zurg.

1552
01:07:41,458 --> 01:07:42,458
(all muttering)

1553
01:07:42,541 --> 01:07:43,750
Well, then, who's this old man?

1554
01:07:43,833 --> 01:07:45,833
(stammers) Why do people keep saying that?

1555
01:07:45,916 --> 01:07:46,916
I'm not that old!

1556
01:07:47,000 --> 01:07:49,833
This old man is a toy.

1557
01:07:49,916 --> 01:07:51,875
Hmm. A toy?

1558
01:07:52,375 --> 01:07:54,708
Yes. We are all toys!

1559
01:07:54,791 --> 01:07:56,333
- Toy…
- (clamoring)

1560
01:07:56,416 --> 01:07:58,875
Our mission on this planet is
to make a child happy.

1561
01:07:58,958 --> 01:07:59,958
I've been dreaming about that.

1562
01:08:00,041 --> 01:08:01,041
You know what I mean?

1563
01:08:01,125 --> 01:08:03,208
- (Buzz) To play!
- To play. Play.

1564
01:08:03,291 --> 01:08:04,375
Hey! Buzz, can you help me…

1565
01:08:04,458 --> 01:08:06,333
(muffled) …get out
of the mouth of this pig?

1566
01:08:06,416 --> 01:08:09,958
Search your feelings, Buzz.
You know it to be true!

1567
01:08:10,041 --> 01:08:12,583
- (Woody groaning)
- (clamoring)

1568
01:08:12,666 --> 01:08:15,875
And the red-haired maiden
you seek is our toy leader.

1569
01:08:15,958 --> 01:08:17,875
Her name is Sheriff Jessie.

1570
01:08:17,958 --> 01:08:18,958
(all) Sheriff Jessie.

1571
01:08:19,041 --> 01:08:22,208
Sheriff Jessie is trapped
inside that stronghold.

1572
01:08:22,291 --> 01:08:24,416
We must infiltrate it and rescue her

1573
01:08:24,500 --> 01:08:25,666
and her trusty steed.

1574
01:08:25,750 --> 01:08:27,083
How do you know all this?

1575
01:08:27,708 --> 01:08:30,083
Because I am her deputy.

1576
01:08:30,166 --> 01:08:31,583
(♪ triumphant music playing)

1577
01:08:31,666 --> 01:08:33,041
(all) Star Command.

1578
01:08:33,125 --> 01:08:36,250
Then this old man is a toy?

1579
01:08:36,333 --> 01:08:38,125
(muffled) This pig has bad breath!

1580
01:08:38,208 --> 01:08:39,291
Oh, yeah, him.

1581
01:08:39,375 --> 01:08:41,416
He's my sidekick. You can untie him.

1582
01:08:41,500 --> 01:08:45,333
And by the way, everybody,
Zurg is our dad.

1583
01:08:45,416 --> 01:08:48,500
- (all) No! No! (sobbing)
- Yeah.

1584
01:08:50,708 --> 01:08:52,708
(♪ adventurous music playing)

1585
01:08:55,666 --> 01:08:57,458
Hey. What's on your mind?

1586
01:08:57,958 --> 01:08:58,958
(Blaze) I don't know.

1587
01:08:59,041 --> 01:09:00,666
I just hope that girl's okay.

1588
01:09:00,750 --> 01:09:03,291
(Blaze's mom) Aw. She'll be fine, sweetie.

1589
01:09:03,375 --> 01:09:04,500
- Don't you worry.
- (door opens)

1590
01:09:04,583 --> 01:09:06,750
Hey, guys! Is anyone hungry?

1591
01:09:06,833 --> 01:09:08,166
- (Blaze) Me, me!
- (Blaze's mom) Starving!

1592
01:09:08,250 --> 01:09:09,833
(Blaze) Can we get Pasta Prairie, Baba?

1593
01:09:09,916 --> 01:09:12,375
(Blaze's dad) Ooh, I like
the way you think, <i>anushikes</i>.

1594
01:09:14,583 --> 01:09:16,791
- (panting)
- Spread out.

1595
01:09:17,500 --> 01:09:18,625
Not here.

1596
01:09:19,166 --> 01:09:20,416
Not here.

1597
01:09:20,500 --> 01:09:21,541
Definitely not here.

1598
01:09:22,333 --> 01:09:23,916
Blast! Where could she be?

1599
01:09:24,000 --> 01:09:26,416
Commander! We found
these electronic devices.

1600
01:09:26,500 --> 01:09:29,541
Hey, Micro-Chippendales!
Hands off. (groans)

1601
01:09:29,625 --> 01:09:31,333
- (chimes)
- Whoa!

1602
01:09:31,416 --> 01:09:33,375
I'm getting a major signal
from all you dudes.

1603
01:09:33,458 --> 01:09:36,250
- I've got full bars.
- Me too. I can map for miles!

1604
01:09:36,333 --> 01:09:38,166
These guys are their own hot spot.

1605
01:09:38,250 --> 01:09:39,625
(beeping)

1606
01:09:39,708 --> 01:09:40,958
Oh, no. They're one of them.

1607
01:09:41,041 --> 01:09:43,750
They're one of us! Nice.

1608
01:09:43,833 --> 01:09:45,250
Hey, uh, this one's broken, by the way.

1609
01:09:45,333 --> 01:09:47,041
Where are you hiding Jessie, you machine?

1610
01:09:47,125 --> 01:09:48,625
Hey, hey. Easy there.

1611
01:09:48,708 --> 01:09:50,250
- Yeah!
- We're Jessie's friends!

1612
01:09:50,333 --> 01:09:52,791
And I have a name. It's Smarty Pants.

1613
01:09:52,875 --> 01:09:54,041
Hygiene instructor.

1614
01:09:54,125 --> 01:09:55,250
He'll wipe your--

1615
01:09:55,333 --> 01:09:57,333
This is serious, Mr. Pants.

1616
01:09:57,416 --> 01:09:59,291
It is my sworn duty as a Space Ranger--

1617
01:09:59,375 --> 01:10:01,416
- Ha, ha, you said "doody."
- Why, you!

1618
01:10:01,500 --> 01:10:03,125
Clearly, we're all friends with Jessie,

1619
01:10:03,208 --> 01:10:05,000
so can you just tell us where she is?

1620
01:10:05,083 --> 01:10:06,500
She went to the tire-swing hill!

1621
01:10:06,583 --> 01:10:07,916
It's at the far end of the ranch.

1622
01:10:08,000 --> 01:10:09,458
Gonna take me forever to waddle there.

1623
01:10:09,541 --> 01:10:11,416
Well, we'll need a way to get there.

1624
01:10:12,125 --> 01:10:13,333
(Buzz Lightyears) Commander Lightyear.

1625
01:10:13,416 --> 01:10:15,416
(♪ uplifting music playing)

1626
01:10:15,500 --> 01:10:16,791
- (gasps)
- Oh, my.

1627
01:10:19,583 --> 01:10:20,833
Whoa.

1628
01:10:30,375 --> 01:10:33,000
Bonnie? Did something happen
with your friends?

1629
01:10:38,458 --> 01:10:39,458
Can you show me?

1630
01:10:41,125 --> 01:10:44,000
You're not in trouble, Bonnie. I promise.

1631
01:10:52,875 --> 01:10:54,083
Oh, sweetie.

1632
01:10:54,666 --> 01:10:58,083
You know that you can always
talk with me and Dad, right?

1633
01:10:58,625 --> 01:11:00,416
About anything.

1634
01:11:00,500 --> 01:11:03,708
Because we love you, Bonnie, so much.

1635
01:11:04,625 --> 01:11:07,416
I wouldn't change
a single thing about you.

1636
01:11:08,083 --> 01:11:10,916
And I think a real friend
would feel the same.

1637
01:11:11,000 --> 01:11:12,000
Don't you?

1638
01:11:13,333 --> 01:11:14,416
But how about we take a break

1639
01:11:14,500 --> 01:11:16,541
from the group chat for now. Okay?

1640
01:11:17,208 --> 01:11:18,416
Let's get some ice cream.

1641
01:11:19,833 --> 01:11:21,333
(sobs)

1642
01:11:27,625 --> 01:11:29,291
Trust me, you're gonna love it.

1643
01:11:29,375 --> 01:11:30,458
(chuckling)

1644
01:11:30,541 --> 01:11:31,750
- Cool! (chuckling)
- Sure.

1645
01:11:35,000 --> 01:11:36,000
(chuckling continues)

1646
01:11:43,416 --> 01:11:46,083
Bonnie, they don't have chocolate chip.

1647
01:11:46,166 --> 01:11:47,750
Come pick another flavor.

1648
01:11:49,041 --> 01:11:51,625
(grunting)

1649
01:11:54,750 --> 01:11:56,166
(panting)

1650
01:12:07,083 --> 01:12:09,333
- (door closes)
- (engine starts)

1651
01:12:09,416 --> 01:12:12,166
- Mom, where's Lilypad?
- (Lilypad panting)

1652
01:12:12,250 --> 01:12:13,958
I'm sorry, Bonnie.

1653
01:12:22,208 --> 01:12:23,500
(creaks)

1654
01:12:31,583 --> 01:12:32,750
(sighs)

1655
01:12:32,833 --> 01:12:34,583
- (♪ suspenseful music plays)
- (grass rustling)

1656
01:12:34,666 --> 01:12:36,041
- (blusters)
- What is it?

1657
01:12:36,125 --> 01:12:37,791
- (♪ triumphant music plays)
- (nickers)

1658
01:12:38,625 --> 01:12:39,625
- (shouts)
- (music ends)

1659
01:12:39,708 --> 01:12:40,958
(grunts) Bullseye.

1660
01:12:41,041 --> 01:12:42,625
You shouldn't have followed me.

1661
01:12:42,708 --> 01:12:45,291
- (nickers)
- Oh, bad horse.

1662
01:12:46,000 --> 01:12:46,833
(blusters)

1663
01:12:47,500 --> 01:12:48,875
(sighs)

1664
01:12:48,958 --> 01:12:52,333
You go back to Blaze's,
Bullseye. You're better off.

1665
01:12:52,416 --> 01:12:54,541
- (♪ somber music plays)
- (whinnies, blusters)

1666
01:12:54,625 --> 01:12:58,041
I'm serious. She'll take good care of you.

1667
01:12:58,125 --> 01:12:59,583
And all those horses…

1668
01:12:59,666 --> 01:13:01,041
(blusters)

1669
01:13:01,125 --> 01:13:02,125
(whinnies)

1670
01:13:03,333 --> 01:13:05,333
(sighs) Bullseye, no.

1671
01:13:05,416 --> 01:13:07,083
I'm not going with you.

1672
01:13:07,583 --> 01:13:09,208
I…

1673
01:13:09,291 --> 01:13:11,375
can't do this again.

1674
01:13:11,458 --> 01:13:12,458
I can't…

1675
01:13:13,625 --> 01:13:15,208
love another kid

1676
01:13:15,291 --> 01:13:17,958
just to find out I never mattered.

1677
01:13:19,666 --> 01:13:20,541
I…

1678
01:13:21,333 --> 01:13:22,958
I can't.

1679
01:13:25,666 --> 01:13:27,958
(blusters)

1680
01:13:30,375 --> 01:13:31,625
(♪ uplifting music plays)

1681
01:13:40,875 --> 01:13:43,583
- (blusters)
- I didn't write that.

1682
01:13:44,416 --> 01:13:45,916
It must have been…

1683
01:14:01,416 --> 01:14:02,416
(gasps)

1684
01:14:02,500 --> 01:14:03,666
Emily?

1685
01:14:04,916 --> 01:14:06,500
(Jessie whistles)

1686
01:14:06,583 --> 01:14:09,083
- Daffodil, dig.
- (whinnies)

1687
01:14:09,166 --> 01:14:10,416
(blusters)

1688
01:14:13,666 --> 01:14:14,666
(blusters)

1689
01:14:14,750 --> 01:14:16,541
(music continues)

1690
01:14:23,083 --> 01:14:24,083
(lock clicks)

1691
01:14:24,166 --> 01:14:26,000
(♪ melancholy music plays)

1692
01:14:26,083 --> 01:14:27,125
Wait.

1693
01:14:28,375 --> 01:14:30,458
This ain't stuff from Emily.

1694
01:14:30,541 --> 01:14:31,541
It…

1695
01:14:32,166 --> 01:14:33,291
It's newer.

1696
01:14:36,000 --> 01:14:37,166
It doesn't make any sense.

1697
01:14:37,250 --> 01:14:39,375
She wouldn't have any of this stuff.

1698
01:14:39,458 --> 01:14:40,958
She'd be…

1699
01:14:44,333 --> 01:14:46,083
all grown-up.

1700
01:14:46,166 --> 01:14:48,000
(♪ uplifting music plays)

1701
01:14:49,541 --> 01:14:50,541
Wait.

1702
01:14:57,375 --> 01:15:00,166
Emily named her daughter…

1703
01:15:04,083 --> 01:15:05,500
after me.

1704
01:15:15,333 --> 01:15:16,666
Really?

1705
01:15:18,666 --> 01:15:20,041
(blusters)

1706
01:15:21,708 --> 01:15:22,708
(nickers)

1707
01:15:24,291 --> 01:15:25,875
(music continues)

1708
01:15:29,166 --> 01:15:30,916
- (grass rustling)
- (blusters)

1709
01:15:31,000 --> 01:15:32,291
- (whinnies)
- (♪ dramatic music plays)

1710
01:15:32,375 --> 01:15:33,708
Uh…

1711
01:15:33,791 --> 01:15:35,666
(screams) Whoa!

1712
01:15:35,750 --> 01:15:37,166
(groans)

1713
01:15:37,250 --> 01:15:38,541
(breathing heavily)

1714
01:15:40,333 --> 01:15:41,666
Jessie? Bullseye!

1715
01:15:41,750 --> 01:15:42,958
- Hey, I found 'em!
- (♪ triumphant music plays)

1716
01:15:43,041 --> 01:15:44,083
Woody?

1717
01:15:45,041 --> 01:15:46,750
- Buzz!
- Jessie!

1718
01:15:46,833 --> 01:15:47,708
(grunts)

1719
01:15:47,791 --> 01:15:48,875
You're okay.

1720
01:15:48,958 --> 01:15:50,958
What… What are you doing here?

1721
01:15:51,041 --> 01:15:52,583
We came for you, Jessie.

1722
01:15:52,666 --> 01:15:53,708
For me?

1723
01:15:53,791 --> 01:15:55,250
We all did.

1724
01:16:03,958 --> 01:16:06,833
Well, howdy-do, Sheriff?

1725
01:16:06,916 --> 01:16:08,208
We come bearing Buzzes.

1726
01:16:08,291 --> 01:16:10,708
Looks like 50 to me,
but I can only count to two.

1727
01:16:10,791 --> 01:16:11,708
(gasps)

1728
01:16:13,083 --> 01:16:15,416
Star Command. Star Command.
Star Command. Star Command.

1729
01:16:15,500 --> 01:16:17,541
Star Command. Star Command. Star Command.

1730
01:16:18,083 --> 01:16:19,416
Star Command.

1731
01:16:19,500 --> 01:16:21,541
All right, all right, calm down.

1732
01:16:21,625 --> 01:16:22,750
Give her some room, fellas.

1733
01:16:22,833 --> 01:16:24,791
- Uh, Buzz.
- Yes?

1734
01:16:24,875 --> 01:16:27,500
Hey, hey, she meant that for me. Just me.

1735
01:16:28,125 --> 01:16:30,375
- We saw Bonnie give you away.
- You did?

1736
01:16:30,458 --> 01:16:31,875
It doesn't make any sense.

1737
01:16:31,958 --> 01:16:33,208
You're not useless, Sheriff!

1738
01:16:33,291 --> 01:16:35,291
- We love you!
- So much!

1739
01:16:35,375 --> 01:16:36,750
(Atlas sobbing)

1740
01:16:36,833 --> 01:16:38,458
(♪ melancholy music plays)

1741
01:16:43,208 --> 01:16:44,583
Look, I'm okay.

1742
01:16:45,250 --> 01:16:48,000
Bonnie's growing up.

1743
01:16:49,208 --> 01:16:54,291
And we don't get to decide
when and how that happens.

1744
01:16:55,541 --> 01:16:56,958
All that matters is

1745
01:16:57,041 --> 01:16:59,000
we were there at the right time

1746
01:16:59,083 --> 01:17:00,750
to help her along.

1747
01:17:00,833 --> 01:17:01,833
(blusters)

1748
01:17:07,625 --> 01:17:09,708
And I gotta believe we were.

1749
01:17:10,875 --> 01:17:12,916
You make us proud to be toys, Jessie.

1750
01:17:13,000 --> 01:17:14,541
- What are you doing? Stop!
- (groaning)

1751
01:17:14,625 --> 01:17:16,625
(clears throat) Sorry, guys. Sorry.

1752
01:17:16,708 --> 01:17:17,708
(blusters)

1753
01:17:17,791 --> 01:17:20,708
Just wish she had at least
connected with Blaze.

1754
01:17:21,666 --> 01:17:22,916
Wait.

1755
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:25,166
- Connect! They still can!
- (♪ upbeat music plays)

1756
01:17:25,250 --> 01:17:26,750
Lilypad can do that!

1757
01:17:26,833 --> 01:17:28,083
- Lilypad?
- Lilypad?

1758
01:17:29,875 --> 01:17:31,666
- (grunts)
- (beeps)

1759
01:17:36,583 --> 01:17:38,250
Okay, okay. Guys, message coming through.

1760
01:17:38,333 --> 01:17:40,250
"Jessie, I'm so sorry.

1761
01:17:40,333 --> 01:17:42,333
Chose wrong friends. Hurt Bonnie."

1762
01:17:42,416 --> 01:17:43,541
- Oh, no.
- Bonnie.

1763
01:17:43,625 --> 01:17:46,166
Smarty, send a reply. "You can fix it."

1764
01:17:49,750 --> 01:17:51,083
- (beeps)
- (gasps)

1765
01:17:51,583 --> 01:17:54,208
"No, I can't. Threw myself away."

1766
01:17:54,291 --> 01:17:55,916
- What?
- "On donation truck."

1767
01:17:56,000 --> 01:17:59,333
Jumpin' Jehoshaphat!
Now she throws herself away?

1768
01:17:59,416 --> 01:18:01,208
(groans) We're goin' after her.

1769
01:18:01,291 --> 01:18:02,500
- What?
- But how?

1770
01:18:02,583 --> 01:18:05,916
Smarty, tell Lily to send
a photo of where she is.

1771
01:18:06,666 --> 01:18:07,666
Got it.

1772
01:18:07,750 --> 01:18:09,625
Snappy, zoom in on that blurry road sign.

1773
01:18:09,708 --> 01:18:11,500
Look at you with that tech talk, cowgirl.

1774
01:18:11,583 --> 01:18:12,791
Martin Avenue.

1775
01:18:12,875 --> 01:18:14,375
Atlas, can you get us to that truck?

1776
01:18:14,458 --> 01:18:16,291
Already mapped it, cowboy lady.

1777
01:18:16,375 --> 01:18:18,666
Tell Lily to keep sending
photos of where she is.

1778
01:18:18,750 --> 01:18:20,083
We're getting her back.

1779
01:18:20,166 --> 01:18:21,500
Yes, Sheriff.

1780
01:18:21,583 --> 01:18:23,083
Jessie, when you have a moment,

1781
01:18:23,166 --> 01:18:24,458
there's something you'd like to ask me…

1782
01:18:24,541 --> 01:18:26,541
- I'd like to ask you.
- Sure thing, Deputy.

1783
01:18:26,625 --> 01:18:28,583
- Now, a little help?
- Yes, Sheriff.

1784
01:18:29,791 --> 01:18:31,541
<i>Yeehaw!</i>

1785
01:18:31,625 --> 01:18:33,083
Let's ride.

1786
01:18:33,166 --> 01:18:34,416
(♪ triumphant music plays)

1787
01:18:34,500 --> 01:18:36,250
Whoa! Hey!

1788
01:18:38,833 --> 01:18:40,541
- Hey! Hey, wait for us!
- Hey! Wait for us!

1789
01:18:40,625 --> 01:18:41,625
(screams)

1790
01:18:41,708 --> 01:18:42,875
- (squeaking)
- (grunts)

1791
01:18:46,583 --> 01:18:47,666
(grunts)

1792
01:18:47,750 --> 01:18:48,833
(breathing heavily)

1793
01:18:49,666 --> 01:18:50,500
(beeps)

1794
01:18:54,416 --> 01:18:56,208
- (music continues)
- She's not far.

1795
01:18:56,291 --> 01:18:59,166
If we go south five blocks,
then east for two,

1796
01:18:59,250 --> 01:19:00,166
we might be able to head 'em off

1797
01:19:00,250 --> 01:19:01,083
before they reach the highway.

1798
01:19:01,166 --> 01:19:02,166
Car!

1799
01:19:02,250 --> 01:19:03,333
(music stops)

1800
01:19:05,541 --> 01:19:07,208
- Clear!
- (music resumes)

1801
01:19:07,708 --> 01:19:08,833
She just passed a gas station.

1802
01:19:08,916 --> 01:19:11,166
(laughs) Passed gas. Sorry, had to.

1803
01:19:11,250 --> 01:19:12,791
We're close. Take a shortcut.

1804
01:19:12,875 --> 01:19:14,208
Down this next road to the right.

1805
01:19:17,250 --> 01:19:18,375
- (squeaks)
- (grunts)

1806
01:19:19,416 --> 01:19:20,250
It's a house!

1807
01:19:20,333 --> 01:19:21,666
I don't get it. There should be a road.

1808
01:19:21,750 --> 01:19:24,000
Probably was a road
five years ago. Old map.

1809
01:19:24,083 --> 01:19:26,333
- Recalculating.
- No time. We're going through.

1810
01:19:26,416 --> 01:19:28,000
- (Buzz) Wait, what?
- (Woody) Going through?

1811
01:19:28,625 --> 01:19:29,916
(music continues)

1812
01:19:36,791 --> 01:19:37,750
(Smarty) Down, boy, down!

1813
01:19:38,541 --> 01:19:39,541
(Woody screams)

1814
01:19:39,625 --> 01:19:41,458
- (screams)
- (Buzz) Whoa, whoa.

1815
01:19:41,541 --> 01:19:42,791
- (Woody grunts)
- (dog barks)

1816
01:19:43,875 --> 01:19:45,083
(barking)

1817
01:19:45,166 --> 01:19:46,500
- Yeehaw!
- (screams)

1818
01:19:46,583 --> 01:19:48,250
- (chicken squawks)
- (Jessie screams)

1819
01:19:48,333 --> 01:19:49,500
(squawking)

1820
01:19:49,583 --> 01:19:50,583
(music continues)

1821
01:19:50,666 --> 01:19:51,750
(coughs)

1822
01:19:52,833 --> 01:19:53,833
(chuckles)

1823
01:19:55,916 --> 01:19:56,916
(shutter clicks)

1824
01:19:57,000 --> 01:20:00,041
The truck. I see it up ahead.

1825
01:20:00,125 --> 01:20:01,541
- (beeping)
- (♪ dramatic music plays)

1826
01:20:01,625 --> 01:20:02,875
Follow me.

1827
01:20:02,958 --> 01:20:04,041
(Buzzes) Yes, Sheriff.

1828
01:20:10,875 --> 01:20:12,916
- (screams)
- (squeaks)

1829
01:20:13,000 --> 01:20:13,833
(Atlas) Whoo!

1830
01:20:13,916 --> 01:20:15,916
We have reached our destination.

1831
01:20:16,000 --> 01:20:17,208
- Lily?
- Lily!

1832
01:20:17,291 --> 01:20:19,125
- Lily, where are ya?
- (Smarty) Lily!

1833
01:20:19,208 --> 01:20:20,708
- (Jessie) Lily?
- Lilypad, where you at?

1834
01:20:20,791 --> 01:20:22,000
Hey, Lily.

1835
01:20:22,083 --> 01:20:23,333
<i>Yes, can I help you?</i>

1836
01:20:24,875 --> 01:20:27,791
Lily. It's okay. We got ya.

1837
01:20:27,875 --> 01:20:29,083
You shouldn't have come, Jessie.

1838
01:20:29,166 --> 01:20:31,166
Nuh-uh. No time for pity parties, Lily.

1839
01:20:31,250 --> 01:20:33,416
Bonnie still needs you to make a friend.

1840
01:20:33,500 --> 01:20:34,458
Me? But I…

1841
01:20:35,458 --> 01:20:38,750
I made a major miscalculation
with Kara, Chelsea and Heidi.

1842
01:20:38,833 --> 01:20:40,666
You were right. Bonnie's different.

1843
01:20:40,750 --> 01:20:41,625
She deserves better.

1844
01:20:41,708 --> 01:20:42,708
Lily.

1845
01:20:42,791 --> 01:20:45,125
You didn't know those girls
were wrong for Bonnie.

1846
01:20:45,208 --> 01:20:46,708
No, I'm wrong for Bonnie.

1847
01:20:46,791 --> 01:20:49,750
- I'm the one who caused this.
- Well, then help me fix it.

1848
01:20:49,833 --> 01:20:52,000
I found Bonnie the right friend.

1849
01:20:52,083 --> 01:20:53,208
- You did?
- Yep.

1850
01:20:53,291 --> 01:20:55,458
So, how about you and me connect them?

1851
01:20:55,541 --> 01:20:57,375
Uh… Okay.

1852
01:20:57,458 --> 01:20:59,625
But first, we gotta get
everyone off this truck

1853
01:20:59,708 --> 01:21:00,750
and back home.

1854
01:21:00,833 --> 01:21:01,791
(screaming)

1855
01:21:01,875 --> 01:21:03,083
(music continues)

1856
01:21:03,916 --> 01:21:05,666
- (horn honks)
- (grunts)

1857
01:21:05,750 --> 01:21:08,333
Uh, we are moving way too fast
to get off now.

1858
01:21:08,416 --> 01:21:10,833
And we're going farther away
by the second.

1859
01:21:10,916 --> 01:21:12,833
There's gotta be something we can do.

1860
01:21:12,916 --> 01:21:15,041
We've got all these fancy Buzzes.

1861
01:21:15,125 --> 01:21:16,291
(gasps)

1862
01:21:17,750 --> 01:21:19,500
Excuse me. Move, move. Out of the way.

1863
01:21:19,583 --> 01:21:20,833
Spaceman, turn around.

1864
01:21:29,041 --> 01:21:31,458
- Snap!
- (gasps) Yes, yes, yes, yes!

1865
01:21:31,541 --> 01:21:32,833
No way.

1866
01:21:32,916 --> 01:21:34,875
Oh, yeah. Way.

1867
01:21:34,958 --> 01:21:36,583
(♪ triumphant music plays)

1868
01:21:39,625 --> 01:21:40,833
Ready, Sheriff?

1869
01:21:40,916 --> 01:21:42,125
Punch it, Lily.

1870
01:21:43,250 --> 01:21:44,916
(electrical humming)

1871
01:21:48,666 --> 01:21:49,666
(radio beeps)

1872
01:21:49,750 --> 01:21:50,833
(whirring)

1873
01:21:56,583 --> 01:21:58,416
Whoa.

1874
01:21:58,500 --> 01:22:00,583
Fly. Be free!

1875
01:22:00,666 --> 01:22:01,666
Show-offs!

1876
01:22:09,375 --> 01:22:11,125
(laughs) Wow.

1877
01:22:11,208 --> 01:22:12,625
Whoo-hoo!

1878
01:22:13,208 --> 01:22:14,541
- Whoo!
- Whoo!

1879
01:22:15,166 --> 01:22:16,166
(laughs)

1880
01:22:16,250 --> 01:22:18,250
Now, this is flying.

1881
01:22:18,333 --> 01:22:19,458
With style!

1882
01:22:19,541 --> 01:22:22,208
Yeehaw!

1883
01:22:27,541 --> 01:22:28,958
So, we're clear on the plan?

1884
01:22:29,041 --> 01:22:31,125
Once you're at Bonnie's,
you send the message.

1885
01:22:31,208 --> 01:22:33,125
Blaze brings me and Bullseye to the house,

1886
01:22:33,208 --> 01:22:35,500
and this time, they connect!

1887
01:22:35,583 --> 01:22:37,708
Jessie, wait.
What if Bonnie rejects you again?

1888
01:22:37,791 --> 01:22:40,416
If they become friends, it's all worth it.

1889
01:22:40,500 --> 01:22:42,000
Yes, Sheriff.

1890
01:22:43,125 --> 01:22:46,083
Huh? Wait. Jessie, wait!

1891
01:22:46,166 --> 01:22:47,250
What?

1892
01:22:48,750 --> 01:22:49,916
What is it, Buzz?

1893
01:22:50,000 --> 01:22:51,125
Just listen to me.

1894
01:22:51,208 --> 01:22:53,166
I… I've been trying
to ask you this, and if…

1895
01:22:53,250 --> 01:22:55,625
if I don't do it now, I never will.

1896
01:22:55,708 --> 01:22:57,708
- (♪ romantic music plays)
- Will you…

1897
01:22:58,208 --> 01:23:00,416
Buzz, you can do this.

1898
01:23:00,500 --> 01:23:01,833
Will… Will…

1899
01:23:04,958 --> 01:23:05,958
(gasps)

1900
01:23:08,000 --> 01:23:10,333
You're stuck with me, Deputy.

1901
01:23:16,041 --> 01:23:17,916
Cheer up, boys. She'll be back.

1902
01:23:18,000 --> 01:23:19,416
We have a plan!

1903
01:23:19,916 --> 01:23:22,541
At ease, Ranger. At ease.

1904
01:23:22,625 --> 01:23:23,500
(music ends)

1905
01:23:29,250 --> 01:23:30,875
(♪ somber music plays)

1906
01:23:38,500 --> 01:23:40,083
(whirring)

1907
01:23:43,125 --> 01:23:44,583
Men, you know your mission.

1908
01:23:44,666 --> 01:23:45,666
Yes, Commander.

1909
01:23:46,583 --> 01:23:47,750
(♪ suspenseful music plays)

1910
01:23:50,291 --> 01:23:51,541
Woody! Buzz!

1911
01:23:51,625 --> 01:23:53,041
- What?
- (Rex) Lily!

1912
01:23:53,125 --> 01:23:54,541
- Oh, no, no, no.
- Foul device.

1913
01:23:54,625 --> 01:23:55,833
What's she doing here?

1914
01:23:55,916 --> 01:23:57,416
She's one of us, guys. Deal with it.

1915
01:23:57,500 --> 01:23:58,500
Listen up, everyone.

1916
01:23:58,583 --> 01:24:00,708
Lily and Jessie
have a plan to help Bonnie.

1917
01:24:00,791 --> 01:24:02,541
Okay, what do you need us to do?

1918
01:24:02,625 --> 01:24:03,500
Nothing.

1919
01:24:03,583 --> 01:24:05,375
- Nothing?
- That's easy.

1920
01:24:05,458 --> 01:24:07,083
Jessie already did the hard work.

1921
01:24:07,166 --> 01:24:08,250
Classic Jessica.

1922
01:24:08,333 --> 01:24:11,375
All that's left for me
is to send a message.

1923
01:24:13,166 --> 01:24:14,250
(whirring)

1924
01:24:14,333 --> 01:24:16,083
(♪ happy music plays)

1925
01:24:26,041 --> 01:24:27,291
(grunts)

1926
01:24:29,416 --> 01:24:31,166
It's up to the girls now.

1927
01:24:32,041 --> 01:24:33,208
(yawns)

1928
01:24:34,000 --> 01:24:35,041
(music continues)

1929
01:24:39,750 --> 01:24:41,208
(gasps)

1930
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:46,500
(giggles)

1931
01:24:51,958 --> 01:24:54,458
Hey, sweetie.
Look what I found in the car.

1932
01:24:54,541 --> 01:24:55,416
(gasps)

1933
01:24:55,500 --> 01:24:57,625
It's okay. We turned off the chat.

1934
01:24:57,708 --> 01:24:59,333
(♪ somber music plays)

1935
01:25:06,625 --> 01:25:08,083
(doorbell rings)

1936
01:25:14,375 --> 01:25:16,750
Bonnie. You have a friend at the door.

1937
01:25:16,833 --> 01:25:17,833
(gasps)

1938
01:25:18,791 --> 01:25:20,166
<i>- Let's try to beat…</i>
<i>- </i>Hi, Bonnie.

1939
01:25:20,250 --> 01:25:22,250
- <i>…our high score.</i>
- I brought your dolls.

1940
01:25:24,000 --> 01:25:25,708
Bonnie, come say hi.

1941
01:25:25,791 --> 01:25:26,833
Okay.

1942
01:25:35,416 --> 01:25:36,458
Hi.

1943
01:25:37,291 --> 01:25:38,291
Hi.

1944
01:25:46,041 --> 01:25:47,916
I'm sorry. I don't play with toys--

1945
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:49,666
I played with her a little yesterday.

1946
01:25:50,500 --> 01:25:52,041
I like it when she's like,

1947
01:25:52,125 --> 01:25:54,041
"I ain't afraid of nothin', partner."

1948
01:25:58,000 --> 01:25:59,000
(chuckles)

1949
01:26:00,750 --> 01:26:02,791
That… That was weird.

1950
01:26:03,291 --> 01:26:04,833
Uh… I…

1951
01:26:05,500 --> 01:26:06,583
Sorry I bothered you.

1952
01:26:11,583 --> 01:26:13,041
- Oh, no. Don't go.
- No, no, no.

1953
01:26:13,125 --> 01:26:14,666
- She can't go. She can't go.
- No, no, no, no.

1954
01:26:16,583 --> 01:26:17,625
Blaze!

1955
01:26:31,166 --> 01:26:34,291
I like your boots.

1956
01:26:37,875 --> 01:26:40,125
I… I really like your socks.

1957
01:26:42,833 --> 01:26:45,625
Do you like my beard, madame?

1958
01:26:46,333 --> 01:26:48,958
Very impressive, m'lady.

1959
01:26:49,041 --> 01:26:51,666
Yes, I'm one billion years old.

1960
01:26:51,750 --> 01:26:53,750
That's why it's so glorious.

1961
01:26:57,916 --> 01:26:59,541
(Bonnie and Blaze laughing)

1962
01:27:01,458 --> 01:27:02,708
Um…

1963
01:27:02,791 --> 01:27:04,375
Do you wanna play?

1964
01:27:04,916 --> 01:27:05,916
(gasps)

1965
01:27:06,791 --> 01:27:07,791
Okay.

1966
01:27:08,875 --> 01:27:10,208
- Walter, let's go.
- Okay. Okay.

1967
01:27:10,291 --> 01:27:12,083
- Do you actually have a horse?
- Yeah.

1968
01:27:12,166 --> 01:27:13,583
(Bonnie) Like, a real one?

1969
01:27:13,666 --> 01:27:15,250
(Blaze laughs) Yes! It's real.

1970
01:27:17,916 --> 01:27:20,416
(gasps) Hey, I have an idea.

1971
01:27:20,500 --> 01:27:21,875
(♪ ceremonial music plays)

1972
01:27:22,875 --> 01:27:24,333
(chattering)

1973
01:27:28,458 --> 01:27:29,458
- (door opens)
- (gasping)

1974
01:27:29,541 --> 01:27:30,875
(gasping, clamoring)

1975
01:27:30,958 --> 01:27:32,541
(Dolly) Look at that kilt.

1976
01:27:34,041 --> 01:27:35,250
(gasps)

1977
01:27:38,208 --> 01:27:40,291
(blusters, cries)

1978
01:27:41,750 --> 01:27:43,208
(sniffling)

1979
01:27:43,291 --> 01:27:45,791
Please, take care of my son.

1980
01:27:49,333 --> 01:27:50,708
(clears throat)

1981
01:27:50,791 --> 01:27:53,791
Friends, we are gathered here today

1982
01:27:53,875 --> 01:27:57,125
to witness the most wonderfulest union

1983
01:27:57,208 --> 01:27:58,541
of Sheriff Jessie

1984
01:27:58,625 --> 01:28:01,291
and Buzz-tholomew MacLightyear.

1985
01:28:01,375 --> 01:28:03,041
- (creaks)
- (beeping)

1986
01:28:09,416 --> 01:28:10,625
Now, Sheriff,

1987
01:28:10,708 --> 01:28:14,500
please put this ring
onto Buzz's itty-bitty finger

1988
01:28:14,583 --> 01:28:16,375
and make your vows.

1989
01:28:17,875 --> 01:28:20,375
Buzz, will you take this ring

1990
01:28:20,458 --> 01:28:22,083
as my pinky promise

1991
01:28:22,166 --> 01:28:25,125
to have fun, and play with you and stuff,

1992
01:28:25,208 --> 01:28:27,083
for all my days,

1993
01:28:27,166 --> 01:28:29,125
even the hard ones?

1994
01:28:29,208 --> 01:28:31,125
- I do--
- (Bonnie's mom) <i>Bonnie…</i>

1995
01:28:31,750 --> 01:28:33,291
have you seen my wedding ring?

1996
01:28:33,375 --> 01:28:34,208
- (gasps)
- (giggles)

1997
01:28:34,291 --> 01:28:35,583
- (giggles)
- (shushes) Uh…

1998
01:28:35,666 --> 01:28:37,625
Maybe check the bathroom?

1999
01:28:37,708 --> 01:28:39,000
Wait, wait, wait. We need, like…

2000
01:28:39,083 --> 01:28:40,250
Flowers! From the garden.

2001
01:28:40,333 --> 01:28:41,750
- Good idea.
- Follow me.

2002
01:28:42,416 --> 01:28:44,500
And there's confetti in the craft drawer.

2003
01:28:45,625 --> 01:28:46,958
Oh, congrats, you two.

2004
01:28:47,041 --> 01:28:48,458
Don't worry. I took plenty of photos

2005
01:28:48,541 --> 01:28:49,625
for Smarty and the gang.

2006
01:28:49,708 --> 01:28:52,416
That's really sweet of you, Lily.

2007
01:28:52,958 --> 01:28:53,958
(chuckles)

2008
01:28:54,041 --> 01:28:55,041
Mmm.

2009
01:28:55,625 --> 01:28:57,041
You done good, Sheriff.

2010
01:28:57,833 --> 01:28:59,750
You can call me Jessica.

2011
01:29:00,291 --> 01:29:01,916
Okay, I will. Jessica.

2012
01:29:02,625 --> 01:29:04,083
Actually, no. No.

2013
01:29:04,166 --> 01:29:05,166
Okay.

2014
01:29:05,250 --> 01:29:06,333
(beeping)

2015
